etrie, z.B. Extremal-/f-Vektor-Fragen, Einsatz topologischer\r\nMethoden, torische und tropische Geometrie, Geometrie der Zahlen etc.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 10, 'ects_str': '10', 'name_str': 'Diskrete Geometrie III', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20160, 'name': 'Besov-Räume, Interpolation und Approximation', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '5', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Besov-Räume, Interpolation und Approximation', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24411}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät II', 'institute': 'Institut für Mathematik', 'group_str': 'Keine Angabe', 'module_description': 'Kenntnis und Verständnis der grundlegenden Techniken und Methoden der Theorie der Besov-Räume\r\nsowie reellen Interpolation zwischen Banach-Räumen und der Approximationstheorie in Banach-Räumen.\r\nDie Teilnehmer sollen die Fähigkeit erwerben, diese auch auerhalb des Rahmens der Vorlesung beispiels-\r\nweise in der Theorie der partiellen Differentialgleichungen anwenden zu können.\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 55% Methodenkompetenz: 30% Systemkompetenz: 10% Sozialkompetenz: 5%\nInterpolation von Banach-Räumen: K-Funktionaltheorie, Reiterations- und Dualitätssatz, Beispiele, Lo-\r\nrentzräume.\r\nBesov-Räume: Definition, Äquivalente Zugänge, Zusammenhang zu Slobodeckij- und Nikolskij-Räumen.\r\nApproximation in Banach-Räumen: Grundlegende Aussagen, Approximationsräume, Ungleichungen von\r\nJackson- und Bernstein. Zusammenhang von Approximations- und Interpolationsräumen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 5, 'ects_str': '5', 'name_str': 'Besov-Räume, Interpolation und Approximation', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20161, 'name': 'Diskrete Strukturen III', 'version': 2, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '10', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Diskrete Strukturen III', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24411}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät II', 'institute': 'Institut für Mathematik', 'group_str': 'Keine Angabe', 'module_description': 'In dieser Veranstaltung werden fortgeschrittene Methoden aus Kombinatorik/Graphentheorie kennenge-\r\nlernt und eingeübt.\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 55% Methodenkompetenz: 30% Systemkompetenz: 10% Sozialkompetenz: 5%\nDie höhere Theorie wird exemplarisch in einem begrenzten Teilgebiet des Bereichs entwickelt. Beispiele\r\nfür solche Teilgebiete sind: "Planare Graphen", "Geordnete Mengen" oder "Randomisierte Methoden".', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 10, 'ects_str': '10', 'name_str': 'Diskrete Strukturen III', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20162, 'name': 'Topologie', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE/EN', 'ects': '10', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Topologie', 'type': 'TUT', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Topologie', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Topologie', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2013', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24397}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24411}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24840}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24858}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät II', 'institute': 'Institut für Mathematik', 'group_str': 'Keine Angabe', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden beherrschen die elementaren Argumentationsweisen der Topologie vor allem bei geo-\r\nmetrischen Problemstellungen.\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 55% Methodenkompetenz: 30% Systemkompetenz: 10% Sozialkompetenz: 5%\nTopologische Räume, Mannigfaltigkeiten, Komplexe, Homotopie und Fundamentalgruppe,\r\nÜberlagerungen, Schnittzahl, Eulercharakteristik und Abbildungsgrad, Elemente einer Homologie-\r\noder Kohomologietheorie.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 10, 'ects_str': '10', 'name_str': 'Topologie', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20163, 'name': 'Theory of Krylov subspace methods', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '5', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Theory of Krylov subspace methods', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24411}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät II', 'institute': 'Institut für Mathematik', 'group_str': 'Keine Angabe', 'module_description': 'Students will master the theoretical background of Krylov subspace methods.\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 65% Methodenkompetenz: 25% Systemkompetenz: 5% Sozialkompetenz: 5%\nThe mathematical principles of Krylov subspace methods, which form an important class of iterative\r\nmethods for solving linear algebraic systems and eigenvalue problems, will be discussed. Different ap-\r\nproaches to the denition and implementation of such methods will be presented, and the connections\r\nto various areas of mathematics will be explored. This will lead to a unied view of important con-\r\ncepts of analysis and algebra. Among the topics are: Projection methods, mathematical characterization\r\nof Krylov subspace methods by their projection properties, implementation of different methods using\r\northogonalization algorithms (in particular Arnoldi and Lanczos algorithms), orthogonal polynomials,\r\nGauss-Christoffel quadrature methods, solution of moment problems, continued fractions, Jacobi matrices\r\nand their algebraic properties, cyclic subspaces and the existence of short recurrences for orthogonalizing\r\nKrylov sequences, error bounds and error estimation in Krylov subspace methods.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 5, 'ects_str': '5', 'name_str': 'Theory of Krylov subspace methods', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20164, 'name': 'Stochastik in den Neurowissenschaften', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '10', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Stochastik in den Neurowissenschaften', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Stochastik in den Neurowissenschaften', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24411}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät II', 'institute': 'Institut für Mathematik', 'group_str': 'Keine Angabe', 'module_description': 'Participants should learn basic concepts, their theoretical foundation, and the most common models of\r\nstochastic processes used in computational neuroscience to model noisy neural systems. Participants will\r\nlearn basic techniques to analyze the stochastic behavior of singles neurons and neural systems both\r\nqualitatively and quantitatively. Participants will also learn basic simulation techniques for stochastic\r\nneural systems and how to evaluate simulation output. Participants should also be able to adapt models\r\nto new problems as well as to develop new models of neural systems.\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 55% Methodenkompetenz: 30% Systemkompetenz: 10% Sozialkompetenz: 5%\nThis module provides basic knowledge about the mathematical modelling, analysis and numerical simu-\r\nlation of neural systems under the in\r\nuence of noise using stochastic processes. Specic topics addressed\r\nare: Brownian motion, stochastic integration, stochastic differential equations, stochastic models for sin-\r\ngle neurons (stochastic integrate-and-re models, random oscillators), coupling of neurons, cooperative\r\nphenomena in neural networks, in particular in stochastic reaction diffusion models (synchronization,\r\nwaves), continuum limits of neural networks', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 10, 'ects_str': '10', 'name_str': 'Stochastik in den Neurowissenschaften', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20165, 'name': 'Stochastic Processes in Evolution', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '5', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Stochastic Processes in Evolution', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24411}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät II', 'institute': 'Institut für Mathematik', 'group_str': 'Keine Angabe', 'module_description': 'Erlernen fortgeschrittener stochastischer Methoden der Populationsgenetik zur Beschreibung evoluti-\r\nonärer Prozesse\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 55% Methodenkompetenz: 30% Systemkompetenz: 10% Sozialkompetenz: 5%\nWright-Fisher Modell, Koaleszenten, genetische Drift, Mutationsmodelle, weitere Themen', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 5, 'ects_str': '5', 'name_str': 'Stochastic Processes in Evolution', 'group': 'Keine Angabe', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Mathematik'}, {'id': 20166, 'name': 'Numerische Mathematik für Ingenieurwissenschaften II (10 LP)', 'version': 2, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '10', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Numerische Mathematik II für Ingenieure', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Numerische Mathematik II für Ingenieure', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 09.01.2012', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 9241}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (B. Sc.) - Bachelor Mathematik 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24377}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsmathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24386}, {'name_degree': 'Mathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24410}, {'name_degr