) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355200 FG S-Professur Neurotechnologie', 'module_description': 'Students having successfully participate in this module are capable of independently \n- pursue investigations in the field of EEG analysis that are relevant for Brain-Computer Interface research,\n- plan and conduct the required experimental studies,\n- evaluate the acquired data using statistical methods, and\n- interpret the results and present them in a scientific way.\n\nThis course conveys predominantly \nprofessional (25%), methods (50%), social (20%), systemic (5%)\nskills.\nThis projects conveys experimental competences of neurotechnology exemplary. Moreover, theoretical skills in signal processing and machine learning are trained practically in hands-on experiments with self acquired data. A typical project is as follows: work out an experimental design for a given hypothesis; implement the experiment and conduct a study (including the acquisition of physiological data) with about 6 participants; investigate the acquire data with standard analysis methods and techniques from machine learning; put the results into perspective given the state-of-the-art and present them as a talk in a written report. Projects are performed in groups of 2 to 4 students.\nNote: This project is about the practical aspects of Brain-Computer Interfaces. The background about this field of research is given in the lecture "Brain-Computer Interfacing".', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Project: Brain-Computer Interfacing', 'group': '34355200 FG S-Professur Neurotechnologie', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40008, 'name': 'Computer Security - Small Project', 'version': 8, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Computer Security Small Project', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'module_description': '1. Understanding of specific features of secure computer systems\n2. Knowledge about vulnerabilities of complex computer systems\n3. A profound evaluation of the security of complex computer systems\nProjects will always be customized regarding the students‘ ideas and offered within the scope of the Computer Security Project. Possible topics include security analysis of embedded systems, protocol analysis and fuzzing, reverse engineering of executables and microkernel/hypervisor improvements.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Computer Security - Small Project', 'group': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40009, 'name': 'Master Project Software Engineering of Embedded Systems', 'version': 5, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Master Project Software Engineering of Embedded Systems', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Automotive Systems (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24775}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351800 FG Software and Embedded Systems Engineering (SESE)', 'module_description': 'Graduates of this module have practical experience with methods and techniques to analyze complex embedded systems. In addition, they have experience with techniques with which the quality or performance of embedded systems can be systematically ensured. They have learned to solve a complex tasks within a team.\nEmbedded systems are often highly complex and safety-critical, for example if they are used in cars, airplanes or avionics. This means that errors can lead to high financial losses or even death or serious injuries. This makes the quality of such systems a major issue and systematic and comprehensive quality assurance techniques are indispensable. In this project, we develop a complex embedded system and use various validation and verification techniques for embedded systems to ensure correctness and performance. As application platform, we use Lego Mindstorm robots.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Master Project Software Engineering of Embedded Systems', 'group': '34351800 FG Software and Embedded Systems Engineering (SESE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40013, 'name': 'Einführung in die Informatik', 'version': 10, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Einführung in die Informatik', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Einführung in die Informatik', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24406}, {'name_degree': 'MINTgrün Orientierungsstudium (OS.) - Studienaufbau MINTgrün', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'O', 'stupo': 24409}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351300 FG Neuronale Informationsverarbeitung', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden werden in die Lage versetzt, ausgehend von einer Problemstellung ein abstraktes Modell zu bilden und dieses auch objektorientiert in einer Programmiersprache zu implementieren. Hierzu werden elementare Programmiertechniken und die Konzepte der Vererbung vermittelt. Die Studierenden erhalten ein Grundwissen im Umgang mit und über den Aufbau von Rechersystemen. Weiter werden die Darstellung von Informationen im Rechner vermittelt. Die Studierenden lernen die Grundlagen von Betriebssystemen kennen. Das vermittelte Grundwissen in Informatik ermöglich den Studierenden dessen Anwendung im eigenen Studienfach und im späteren Berufsleben.\n1) Programmieren in der Sprache Java (Economics, Volkswirtschaftslehre), C/C++ (Elektrotechnik) oder einer davon nach Wahl (andere Studiengänge):\r\n 1) Datentypen, Arrays, Zeichenketten\r\n 2) Bezeichner, Variablen, Ausdrücke, Gültigkeitsbereiche, Referenzen \r\n 3) Statische Methoden, Funktionen\r\n 4) Bedingte Ausführung, Schleifen, Rekursionen \r\n 5) Objektorientierung, Attribute, Objektmethoden\r\n 6) Vererbung, Konstuktoren, Polymorphie, abstrakte Klassen\r\n\r\n2) Rechneraufbau:\r\n 1) Darstellung von Zahlen und Zeichen im Rechner\r\n 2) Logische Schaltungen, Addierer, Speicherzellen, Flip-Flops\r\n 3) Rechnersysteme, Prozessor & Prozesse, Arbeitspeicher, Betriebsystem', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Einführung in die Informatik', 'group': '34351300 FG Neuronale Informationsverarbeitung', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40014, 'name': 'Einführung in die Informatik - Vertiefung', 'version': 5, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Einführung in die Informatik - Vertiefung', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Einführung in die Informatik - Vertiefung', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'MINTgrün Orientierungsstudium (OS.) - Studienaufbau MINTgrün', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'O', 'stupo': 24409}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Computational Engineering Science (Informationstechnik im Maschinenwesen) (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24821}], 'exam