tupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'module_description': "In this seminar, students will be introduced to an advanced topic in data management (e.g., data cleaning). Students will learn how to critically read scientific materials drawn from the database and information systems literature.\nStudents will also learn about the core elements of a technical presentation and have an opportunity to sharpen their critical thinking skills. Furthermore, students will learn how to write a technical report.\nDuring the initial weeks, students will be offered lectures on the core elements of a technical presentation, how to offer an effective presentation, how to critically read scientific papers, and how to write a technical report. In addition, each seminar participant will be assigned a scientific topic as well as reading materials (e.g., drawn from a textbook on advanced data management, database systems, or data science technologies and systems). In the subsequent weeks, each student will read their assigned reading materials and study them deeply, in order to assemble and deliver their own presentation. Moreover, each week, students will be required to reflect on the main challenges addressed in each of their peers' presentations. (Details will be announced in the class.)", 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'DBSEM - Seminar on Advanced Topics in Database and Information Systems', 'group': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40404, 'name': 'Datenkompression', 'version': 6, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Quellencodierung', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Statistische Nachrichtentheorie', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Audiokommunikation und -technologie (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24387}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331100 FG Nachrichtenübertragung', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden besitzen vertiefte Kenntnisse auf dem Gebiet der Datenkompression von Multimediasignalen. Sie können wissenschaftliche\r\nFragestellungen/ Thesen in diesem Feld formulieren und systematisch Ergebnisse zur Validierung der\r\nThese produzieren und veröffentlichen. Sie sind befähigt eigenständig Forschungsansätze zu verfolgen\r\nund fremde wissenschaftliche Texte zu kritisieren.\nDie wachsende Nachfrage nach einer effizienten und zuverlässigen Übertragung von Daten-, Sprach-, Audio- und Bildsignalen stellt insbesondere in mobilen Kommunikationsnetzen mit deren beschränkter Bandbreite, hohe Anforderungen an die Nachrichtenübertragungssysteme. Einen wesentlichen Anteil zur Reduzierung der Datenmenge leistet die Quellencodierung.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Datenkompression', 'group': '34331100 FG Nachrichtenübertragung', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 40405, 'name': 'DBT Database Technology', 'version': 11, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'DBT: Database Technology', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24597}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramtsbezogen) (MEd) - Anlage 3 - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24761}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Computational Engineering Science (Informationstechnik im Maschinenwesen) (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24821}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'module_description': 'The global data volume is increasing dramatically each year. Understanding how to store, process and manage these huge amounts of data efficiently is a key requirement for software engineers and data analysts in the modern IT world. This course will teach students both the fundamentals of data processing in traditional single-node database systems and how to scale out these techniques to huge amounts of data in large-scale, distributed environments.\nThe database technology course will teach the students about the internals of a database management system. The students will learn the fundamentals of database technology for relational database systems. This includes the general architecture of a DBMS, file- and buffer management, data layouts and representation, caching and indexing, index structures, query processing, metadata management, query optimization, locking, recovery and transaction management.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'DBT Database Technology', 'group': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40407, 'name': 'Digital Communities', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Digital Communities', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34335700 FG S-Professur Service Centric Networking (SNET)', 'module_description': 'Students who have successfully finished this module have an overview of current and future concepts of digital communities, specifically of the architectural aspects they are based on. They have acquired a deep understanding of both low and high level aspects of decentralized OSN services and are able to apply the various concepts for creating novel OSN platforms.\nThe module starts with an introduction to the fundamentals of digital communities and an overview of historical and contemporary online social networks (OSN) and the technological challenges and problems they face. The second part of the module discusses architectures, standards, and protocols of the social web with a clear focus on decentralized and distributed online social networks. This includes architectural concepts for federated, peer-topeer, and blockchain-based online social network architectures as well as the standards and protocols implemented for inter-platform communication and collaboration. For example, architectures and protocols of various peer-topeer systems and Blockchains are analyzed and discussed. The third part of the module focuses on decentralized identity management (IDM), discussing various aspects of IDM and existing established and novel services, such as the Domain Name Service (DNS), the Ethereum Name Service (ENS), or Self-Sovereign Identity (SSI).\n\nFinally, the module gives an introduction to graph theory, followed by methods and applications of social network analysis. The module aims to present a holistic view of the different parts, discussing historic, current state-of-the-art, and novel standards and systems. If applicable, scientific literature (papers) and live coding examples are used during the lecture. Students who have successfully finished this module have an overview of current and future concepts of digital communities, specifically of the architectural aspects they are based on. They have acquired a deep understanding of both low and high level aspects of decentralized OSN services and are able to apply the various concepts for creating novel OSN platforms.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Digital Communities', 'group': '34335700 FG S-Professur Service Centric Networking (SNET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 40413, 'name': 'Digitale Systeme', 'version': 5, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Digitale Systeme', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Digitale Systeme', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2013', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24397}, {'name_degree': 'MINTgrün Orientierungsstudium (OS.) - Studienaufbau MINTgrün', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'O', 'stupo': 24409}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24545}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24595}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24596}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramtsbezogen) (MEd) - Anlage 3 - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24761}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24840}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24858}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24890}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24891}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355300 FG S-Professur Quality and Usability', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden sind in der Lage, die Grundkenntnisse im Bereich digitaler Logikschaltungen mit Bezug zu physikalischen Leistungsparametern zu reflektieren und beherrschen die wichtigsten Begriffe,\r\nEigenschaften und Theorien sowie die elementaren Komponenten und Konstruktionsprinzipien digitaler Schaltungen. Sie besitzen die Fertigkeit zum Entwurf von Schaltnetzen und Schaltwerken und sind zur Teamarbeit in Kleingruppen fähig.\n• Kenngrößen digitaler Schaltungen\r\n• Schaltalgebra\r\n• Schaltungsprinzipien für Logikfunktionen\r\n• Schaltnetze wichtiger Funktionen\r\n• Flipflops\r\n• Schaltwerke\r\n• Arithmetische Schaltungen, ALU\r\n• Programmierbare Logikschaltungen', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Digitale Systeme', 'group': '34355300 FG S-Professur Quality and Usability', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40414, 'name': 'Digital Image Processing', 'version': 10, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Digital Image Processing', 'type': 'VL', 'cyc