0 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'module_description': 'Students who have successfully finished this module have an advanced knowledge of operating systems for embedded systems. They are aware of the specific design aspects (like realtime behavior, energy consumption, schedulability, fault tolerance) and know of their interdependencies.\nEmbedded OS: Requirements for embedded systems; example application areas; embedded processor architecture; realtime scheduling; worst case execution time estimation, schedulability analysis;\nDependable Systems: Basic notions and quantities, failure models, fault trees, availability analysis for composition, Byzantine protocols.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Dependable Embedded Systems', 'group': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40441, 'name': 'Embedded Systems Security Lab', 'version': 7, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Security Lab', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'module_description': 'This module’s qualification aims are:\r\n1. Understanding of security relevant interfaces (hard- and software) of (embedded) computer systems\r\n2. Practical experience in identifying, exploiting, and fixing of vulnerabilities in hard- and software\r\n3. A profound evaluation of system security\nThe security lab offers students the opportunity to learn how to analyze the system security of embedded systems. It covers topics from hardware security and debug facilities and then moves on to software security issues in applications, the kernel and messaging handling drivers. This course focuses on practically relevant details and hands-on experience instead of providing thorough theoretical background information.\r\n\r\nStudents will have to solve multiple challenges, where a system has to be analyzed and then compromised. Basic Linux and C programming knowledge is required.\r\nThe lab is organized as a practical course (PR) and students will be working individually with an ARM development board (Raspberry Pi II).\r\n\r\nTOPICS:\r\n• Serial interface\r\n• ARM introduction\r\n• JTAG hardware debugging interface\r\n• OpenOCD, BusPirate\r\n• Software debugging with GDB\r\n• Linux security tools\r\n• Public key cryptography, certificates and signatures\r\n• Shellcode\r\n• Memory corruption vulnerabilities\r\n• NX/XD/XN, ASLR, stack canaries\r\n• ELF binary format\r\n• Heap structure\r\n• Integer overflows\r\n• Kernel security', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Embedded Systems Security Lab', 'group': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40448, 'name': 'Entwurf eingebetteter Systeme', 'version': 7, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Entwurf eingebetteter Systeme', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Entwurf eingebetteter Systeme', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2013', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24397}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24597}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramtsbezogen) (MEd) - Anlage 3 - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24761}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24840}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24858}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351800 FG Software and Embedded Systems Engineering (SESE)', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden haben praktische Erfahrung im Einsatz von Methoden und Techniken zum Entwurf eingebetteter Systeme. Sie sind darin geübt, solche Aufgabenstellungen im Team zu lösen.\nEs werden Methoden und Techniken zum Entwurf sicherer und effizienter eingebetteter Systeme\r\ngeübt. Als Beispiel dient der Entwurf eines ausführbaren Modells eines komplexen eingebetteten Systems, z.B. einer typischen Steuerung aus dem Transport- und Logistikbereich oder verwandten Gebieten. Ausgehend von einer abstrakten Systemspezifikation, in der Prozesse und deren Synchronisation und Zeitverhalten beschrieben werden, soll ein ausführbares Modell der Hardware- und Software-Anteile entworfen und implementiert werden. Als Anwendungsplattform dienen Lego Mindstorm Roboter.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Entwurf eingebetteter Systeme', 'group': '34351800 FG Software and Embedded Systems Engineering (SESE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40458, 'name': 'Game Programming', 'version': 7, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Game Programming', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341300 FG Computer Graphics', 'module_description': 'Students have basic knowledge in computer game development and can put into practice the acquired knowledge and skills in programming and graphic design of computer games.\nThis module provides an insight into the creation of computer games and current developments in this area. The participants develop game prototypes in small groups. Progress, difficulties and problems are presented and discussed at regular intervals.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Game Programming', 'group': '34341300 FG Computer Graphics', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 40461, 'name': 'Structural Graph Theory', 'version': 2, 'language': 'DE/EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352200 FG Logik und Semantik', 'module_description': 'Students completing the course will understand how structural information about instances to computational problems can be used in the design of efficient algorithms. They will be familiar with basic nations of graph decompositions and the \r\nalgorithmic techniques facilitated to use this additional information.\nMany algorithmic problems on graphs are NP-hard and therefore there is good evidence that no efficient algorithms solving these problems on all graphs exist. Classical examples are routing problems arising e.g. in integrated circuit layout and\r\n design, colouring problems in scheduling applications or domination problems in facility location.\r\n\r\nHowever, instances to these problems arising in practical applications may have more ”structure“ than general graphs, e.g. instances may be “hierarchical” or “tree-like”. Using this additional structural information may help in designing efficient\r\n algorithms for solving problems in instances of this form.\r\n\r\nA particularly good example are instances which are planar graphs, i.e. graphs that can be drawn without crossing edges. Planar graphs arise for instance in routing applications, as many road or train maps are nearly planar. It turns out that if the input instance is planar, or a tree, then many hard problems become tractable.\r\n\r\nIn this course we will study methods for solving algorithmic problems on restricted classes of graphs. The most important cases will be planar graphs and graph classes defined by the concept of bounded tree-width. We will then extend this to even more general classes of graphs.\r\n\r\nThe focus of this lecture is to introduce the structural properties of graphs that can be employed in the design of efficient algorithms and to present the algorithmic techniques needed for this.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Structural Graph Theory', 'group': '34352200 FG Logik und Semantik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40462, 'name': 'Großes Projekt Messdatenverarbeitung', 'version': 5, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Großes Projekt Messdatenverarbeitung', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name