', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramtsbezogen) (MEd) - Anlage 3 - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24761}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24890}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24891}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355300 FG S-Professur Quality and Usability', 'module_description': 'Students gain\n- Understanding of “Usability” as inter-disciplinary research and application area in the development of information and communication technologies\n- Fundamental knowledge of multimodal human-computer interaction\n- Knowledge of the implementation of human-computer interfaces\n- Knowledge of methods for measuring quality and usability\n- Presentation of knowledge to an audience\nCurrent topics in the research area of quality and usability will be discussed and applied to practical problems.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Quality & Usability', 'group': '34355300 FG S-Professur Quality and Usability', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40662, 'name': 'Quality Assurance of Embedded Systems', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Quality Assurance of Embedded Systems', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351800 FG Software and Embedded Systems Engineering (SESE)', 'module_description': 'Graduates of this module are able to master methods and techniques with which the quality of embedded systems can be systematically ensured, in particular fault-tolerance, computer-aided verification and test automation techniques. They have knowledge about existing techniques and know how to apply them.\nEmbedded systems are often safety-critical, for example if they are used in cars, airplanes or avionics. This means that errors can lead to high financial losses or even death or serious injuries. This makes the quality of such systems a major issue and systematic and comprehensive quality assurance techniques are indispensable. In this course, we consider quality assurance for embedded systems ranging from validation and testing over computer-aided verification to system verification and HW/SW co-verification. As a formal foundation, the course introduces formal specification techniques like Timed Automata, and temporal logics. Using this formal foundation, the main focus of the course is on analytical quality assurance, i.e., computer-aided verification via model checking and automated testing (coverage-driven input selection, automated test pattern generation, conformance testing ...). Additionally, we consider runtime monitoring and adaptation techniques for fault-tolerance.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Quality Assurance of Embedded Systems', 'group': '34351800 FG Software and Embedded Systems Engineering (SESE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40663, 'name': 'Usability Engineering in Information and Communication Technologies', 'version': 4, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Usability Engineering', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Human Factors (MSc) - StuPO 2011', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 21561}, {'name_degree': 'Human Factors (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24815}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355300 FG S-Professur Quality and Usability', 'module_description': 'The students gain:\r\n- Comprehension of  „Usability“ as interdisciplinary research and application field at the development of Information and Communication Technologies.\r\n- Basic knowledge of the processes of human perception and judgement that are a crucial factor for the quality and usability of information and communication technologies.\r\n- Basic knowledge of multimodal human-machine interaction.\r\n- Knowledge of methods for measuring quality and usability.\r\n- Competence in the presentation of the learned knowledge to others\r\n\r\nThe students know:\r\n- how to apply this knowledge in the design cycle of technical systems\r\n- how to apply the learned methods for the judgement of quality and usability of selected technical systems.\nIV „Usability Engineering“:\r\nTerms of quality, usability and human engineering; Psychophysics and psychometrics basics; Measurement and prediction of quality; Scaling; Quality units and characteristics; Usability Engineering Lifecycle; Usability heuristics; Usability tests; Usability evaluation methods; Quality of graphical interfaces; Quality of transmission systems; Quality of interactive systems; Quality prediction models; Standards', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Usability Engineering in Information and Communication Technologies', 'group': '34355300 FG S-Professur Quality and Usability', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40664, 'name': 'Current trends in graph theory and combinatorics', 'version': 3, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Graphsuch-Spiele', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'k.A.'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352200 FG Logik und Semantik', 'module_description': 'Students will have gained a broader overview of recent results and developments in graph theory/combinatorics.\nThis seminar covers recent developments and results in graph theory or combinatorics/discrete maths. Students can choose among a selection of papers and then present the background, main result and proof ideas of their chosen topic in an oral presentation.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Current trends in graph theory and combinatorics', 'group': '34352200 FG Logik und Semantik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40667, 'name': 'Randomized Algorithmics', 'version': 7, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Randomized Algorithmics', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'k.A.'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351100 FG Algorithmik und Komplexitätstheorie', 'module_description': 'Participants of this module know fundamental randomized methods for design and analysis of efficient algorithms. They can perform simple probabilistic analyses and are aware of the limitations of randomization.\nIntroduction into the mathematical and algorithmic foundations of algorithm design and analysis using the resource "random bits".\nParticular topics are:\n- randomized algorithms for graph problems and geometric problems\n- the probabilistic method\n- randomized complexity classes', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Randomized Algorithmics', 'group': '34351100 FG Algorithmik und Komplexitätstheorie', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40668, 'name': 'Recent Advances in Computer Architecture', 'version': 3, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Recent Advance in Computer Architecture', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341400 FG Architektur eingebetteter Systeme', 'module_description': 'After completion participants will have acquired the necessary knowledge and skills to read, discuss, understand, present, and summarize original research in the field of computer architecture and follow original research talks. They are able to provide feedback on each other’s work and to formulate research questions. They are further able to write a review paper about recent developments in computer architecture.\nIn this seminar we will study the proceedings of top computer architecture conferences (for example, Int. Symp. On Computer Architecture (ISCA) and the Int. Symp. On Microarchitecture (MICRO)) and journals, make a selection of the papers, and present and discuss these papers in class.\r\nWe will also write a review paper about the related papers.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Recent Advances in Computer Architecture', 'group': '34341400 FG Architektur eingebetteter Systeme', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 40672, 'name': 'Rechnernetze und Verteilte Systeme', 'version': 12, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Rechnernetze und verteilte Systeme', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Rechnernetze und verteilte Systeme', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2013', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24397}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramtsbezogen) (MEd) - Anlage 3 - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24761}, {'name_degree': 'Computational Engineering Science (Informationstechnik im Maschinenwesen) (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24821}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24840}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24858}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331200 FG Telekommunikationsnetze', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden verstehen das Prinzip hinter der Schichtenarchitektur von Netzwerkprotokollen und können beschreiben welche Aufgaben die jeweilige Schicht im OSI-Modell erfüllt. Des Weiteren sind sie in der Lage die Funktionsweise der wichtigsten Protokolle des Internets (u.a. Ethernet, IP, DNS, TCP, UDP) zu beschreiben. Darüber hinaus können die Studierenden darstellen welche Vorteile eine verteilte Netzwerkarchitektur bietet, welche Herausforderungen es beim Entwurf von verteilten Systemen gibt (u.a. Zeitsynchronisation, Konsens, atomizität von Transaktionen) und sie können Algorithmen beschreiben um diese Probleme zu lösen.\nDas Praktikum befähigt die Studenten einfache Netzwerkanwendungen mit Hilfe der Berkeley-Socket-API zu entwickeln in der Programmiersprache C, wodurch Sie in der Lage sind die kennengelernten Algorithmen eigenständig in die Praxis umzusetzen.\n* Prinzipien der Verteiltheit\n * Inter-Prozess-Kommunikationsparadigmen (mit Sockets sowie komplexen Interaktionsmodellen)\n * Lokale Netze im Internet; Beispiele: Ethernet und WLAN\n * Prinzipien des Internetprotokollstack: TCP, UDP/RTP, IP\n * Mechanismen der Vernetzung: Vermittlungsverfahren, Fehlerkontrolle, Routing\n * Strukturierung des Zugriffs auf Dienste (Client-Server, Peer-to-peer)\n * Middleware\n * Webdienste\n * Fundamentale Fragestellungen in verteilten Systemen: Zeitsynchronisation, Consensus, Transaktionen\n\nEin wesentlicher Aspekt des Moduls Rechnernetze und Verteilte Systeme ist es, die Vorteile von dezentralen, verteilten Systemen zu erläutern. Dabei wird an mehreren Stellen auf die gesellschaftlichen Folgen von zentralisierter Infrastruktur eingegangen und die Frage gestellt, warum es Teil der Philosophie des Internets ist, Machtkonzentration mit technischen Mitteln zu vermeiden. (Insbesondere wird dies in den Vorlesungsblöcken zum Thema Peer-to-Peer Kommunikation und DNS & WWW behandelt.)', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Rechnernetze und Verteilte Systeme', 'group': '34331200 FG Telekommunikationsnetze', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 40676, 'name': 'Regelungstechnik', 'version': 7, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Grundlagen der Regelungstechnik', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 09.01.2012', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 9241}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24406}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24463}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24597}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik/Informationstechnik als Quereinstieg (Lehramtsbezogen) (MEd) - Anlage 3 - StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24761}, {'name_degree': 'Automotive Systems (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24775}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24897}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34311800 FG Regelungssysteme (Control Systems)', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden besitzen einen Überblick über grundlegende Methoden der Regelungstechnik zur Modellierung, Analyse und Synthese von Regelkreisen und können diese anwenden. Durch Übungen und Anwendungsbeispiele innerhalb eines Praktikums können die Teilnehmenden nach Abschluss des Moduls praktische Probleme selbständig durch Anwendung von Softwaretools lösen.\nWiederholung Signale und Systeme, Systembeschreibung im Zeit- und Frequenzbereich, Stabilität, quantitative Regelkreiseigenschaften, Grenzen erreichbarer Regelkreiseigenschaften, Robustheit, Reglerentwurf mit Frequenzgangsmethoden, Wurzelortskurvenmethode, algebraischer Reglerentwurf, Regelkreise mit Totzeit. Das Modul enthält auch Inhalte zur gesellschaftlichen Verantwortung und Nachhaltigkeit bzw. zur Technikfolgenabschätzung, insbesondere zur Notwendigkeit von Regelung bei der verstärkten Einbindung erneuerbarer Energien in das Stromnetz.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Regelungstechnik', 'group': '34311800 FG Regelungssysteme (Control Systems)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 40682, 'name': 'Renewable Energy for Sustainable Electric Networks', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Renewable Energy Integration in Electric Networks', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34312000 FG Energieversorgungsnetze und Integration Erneuerbarer Energien (SENSE)', 'module_description': 'Upon successful completion of the module Renewable Energy for Sustainable Electric Networks participants will have engineering competence on grid integration of renewable energy and the sustainable energy systems and controls involved. The focus is on the behavior of renewable energy sources in the grid during normal operation and in case of a fault. This will help students to design efficient and grid-compatible solutions for the integration of renewable energy sources. The module further gives a comprehensive insight into renewable energy technology, which is of great importance to the understanding of grid integration.\nIn the course "Renewable Energy Integration in Electric Networks" (REI) the learning will be supported by a model-based approach. Models of renewable energy systems in the grid will be developed step by step. This includes the conversion stages from the source to the grid. Different types of system dynamics are considered. Control systems are designed. Smart grid topics such as virtual power plants and microgrids are discussed. \r\n\r\nThe course "Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks" (RET) covers the topic of renewable resources, including wind, sun, tides and biomass as well as their significance for energy supply. The learning will be supported by a model-based approach. At the beginning, the focus lies on a photovoltaic plant. The modeling comprises irradiation and maximum-power-point-tracking. Furthermore, the modeling of wind energy conversion systems is considered. Other topics include battery application, fuel cells, and tidal energy.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Renewable Energy for Sustainable Electric Networks', 'group': '34312000 FG Energieversorgungsnetze und Integration Erneuerbarer Energien (SENSE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 40683, 'name': 'Renewable Energy Integration in Electric Networks', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Renewable Energy Integration in Electric Networks', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34312000 FG Energieversorgungsnetze und Integration Erneuerbarer Energien (SENSE)', 'module_description': 'Upon successful completion of the module Renewable Energy Integration in Electric Networks, participants will have important engineering competence on grid integration of renewable energy. The focus is on dynamic behavior of renewable energy sources in the grid during normal operation and in case of a fault. This will help students to design efficient and grid-compatible solutions for the integration of renewable energy.\nThe content is developed through a model-based approach. Models for renewable energy systems in the grid will be developed step by step. This includes the conversion stages from the source to the grid. Different types of system dynamics are considered. Control systems are designed. Smart grid topics such as virtual power plants and microgrids are discussed.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Renewable Energy Integration in Electric Networks', 'group': '34312000 FG Energieversorgungsnetze und Integration Erneuerbarer Energien (SENSE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 40684, 'name': 'Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Regenerative Energiesysteme (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2009', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 8581}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24795}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34312000 FG Energieversorgungsnetze und Integration Erneuerbarer Energien (SENSE)', 'module_description': 'Upon successful completion of the module Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks, participants will have comprehensive knowledge of relevant technologies and systems of renewable energy sources and storage. Students will get to know the modeling and control of renewable energy technology, which is of great importance for the understanding of grid integration.\nThe course "Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks" covers the topic of renewable resources, including wind, sun, tides and biomass as well as their significance for energy supply. The learning will be supported by a model-based approach. At the beginning, the focus lies on the control of a photovoltaic plant. The modeling comprises irradiation and maximum-power-point-tracking. Furthermore, the modeling of wind energy conversion systems is considered. Other topics include battery application, fuel cells, and tidal energy.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Renewable Energy Technology in Electric Networks', 'group': '34312000 FG Energieversorgungsnetze und Integration Erneuerbarer Energien (SENSE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 40685, 'name': 'Research Colloquium on Algorithms and Complexity', 'version': 9, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Research Colloquium on Algorithms and Complexity', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'paper', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351100 FG Algorithmik und Komplexitätstheorie', 'module_description': 'Participants of this module have learned how to critically read and evaluate scientific papers. They are able to work independently to gain an understanding of current research results and the methods and proofs behind. They can communicate the central ideas behind and discuss the value of the presented findings. They know about the key features of good oral presentations.\nIn this seminar recent research of our group and special invited guests is presented. The main topics arise from algorithms, complexity, and corresponding applications. The seminar is an excellent opportunity for advanced students to get in touch with current topics in our research field, or to present their own results in this context.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Research Colloquium on Algorithms and Complexity', 'group': '34351100 FG Algorithmik und Komplexitätstheorie', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 40686, 'name': 'Robotics', 'version': 17, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Robotics', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 09.01.2012', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 9241}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24795}, {'name_degree': 'Computational Engineering Science (Informationstechnik im Maschinenwesen) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018 (17.01.2018)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24859}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24897}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'module_description': 'After completing the module, the students will have knowledge of the problems and practical solutions to controlling multi-joint robot systems. They will also have acquired methods to abstract and simplify complex, non-linear problems in the realm of action, perception, and representation, which are the basis for cognitive and intelligent robots.\nConcepts, algorithms and application-specific aspects of Robotics:\n- Kinematics, dynamics, position control, trajectory generation, controller tuning, collision avoidance, visual servoing, probabilistic robotics, Simultaneous Localization and Mapping (SLAM).\n- Practical implementation on a real time control system.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Robotics', 'group': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 40687, 'name': 'Robotics: Advanced', 'version': 4, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Robotics', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'module_description': 'Studierende erhalten ein tiefes Verständnis in Probleme und Methoden der Robotik im Kontext von embodied intelligence. Sie sind in der Lage, etablierte und neuartige Konzepte und Methoden kritisch zu betrachten und anzuwenden.\nMethoden, Algorithmen und Grenzen des Stands der Technik im Greifen, Kollisionsvermeidung, Kraftregelung, integrierte Bahnplanung und Regelung, Visuelle Wahrnehmung, Repräsentation von Raum und Maschinelles Lernen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Robotics: Advanced', 'group': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 40688, 'name': 'Robotics I+II', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Robotics', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Robotics', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'module_description': 'After completing the module, the students have knowledge of problems and practical solutions to controlling multi-joint robot systems. They also have acquired methods to abstract and simplify complex, non-linear problems in the realm of action, perception, and representation, which are the basis for cognitive and intelligent robots.\r\n\r\nStudents will also have gained a deeper understanding of problems and methods in robotics (in the context of embodied intelligence).  After completing the course, students will be able to critically assess and use established concepts and methods as well as novel ones.\nRobotics I + II is composed of the two courses "Robotics" and "Robotics: Advanced" with the following content.\r\n\r\nConcepts, algorithms and application specific aspects of Robotics:\r\nkinematics, dynamics, position control, trajectory generation, controller tuning, collision avoidance, visual servoing, probabilistic robotics Simultaneous Localization and Mapping (SLAM).\r\nPractical implementation on a real time control system.\r\n\r\nMethods, algorithms, and limits of state of the art solutions in grasping, collision avoidance, force control, integrated planning and control, visual perception, representations of space, and machine learning.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Robotics I+II', 'group': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 40689, 'name': 'Robotics: Project', 'version': 12, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Robotics: Project', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'module_description': "After attending the module, students possess in-depth knowledge of specific topics in ongoing, state-of-the-art robotics research. Students\ngain both theoretical knowledge and practical experience, and, where appropriate, conduct real-robot experiments to develop and validate their research\nideas. They know how to organize, track and adapt a project to resource constraints. They know how to work independently towards a project objective while balancing scientific and practical objectives. \nStudents possess skills in project planning, giving project presentations, discussing project ideas in a team, writing scientific reports, and documenting source code for use by others.\nVarying topics from robotics and related fields of research, e.g., machine learning, perception, motion planning, manipulation, control, and hardware design.\nProject topics are tightly coupled with the department's ongoing research activities. Therefore, we encourage prospective students to visit the department's website to learn about possible project topics:\nhttps://www.robotics.tu-berlin.de/menue/research/", 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Robotics: Project', 'group': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 40693, 'name': 'Data Science Project', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Data Science Project', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361200 FG Agententechnologien in betrieblichen Anwendungen und der Telekommunikation (AOT)', 'module_description': 'Graduates of the module have gained practical experience in dealing with complex data science problems. They are able to formulate scientific questions and systematically validate them using empirical evaluations on datasets. Graduates can formulate and present the results of the examination according to scientific standards. They are able to pursue independent research approaches and to criticize foreign scientific texts.\nIn this course, a data science problem from a scientific or industrial domain is treated in a practice-oriented manner. The aim of the project is to formulate and validate a scientific question. For this purpose, own approaches to solving the problem are developed and implemented. The approach and the results of the validation are documented in a scientific report and presented in a presentation. Students deal in particular with the following topics:\r\n\r\n- Machine Learning\r\n- Feature Extraction\r\n- Deep Learning\r\n- Data Preprocessing\r\n- Model Evaluation\r\n- Machine Learning Libraries\r\n- Scientific Writing', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Data Science Project', 'group': '34361200 FG Agententechnologien in betrieblichen Anwendungen und der Telekommunikation (AOT)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 40696, 'name': 'Seminar Mess- und Diagnosetechnik', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Seminar Mess- und Diagnosetechnik', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Automotive Systems (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24775}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34311600 FG Elektronische Mess- und Diagnosetechnik', 'module_description': 'Students are able to do a literature research, to summarize the results scientifically, to present and to defend their work.\nResults of new research on the field of measurement and diagnostic technology, modeling and simulation are recited in presentations and papers. The main focus lies on vehicle and engine development.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Seminar Mess- und Diagnosetechnik', 'group': '34311600 FG Elektronische Mess- und Diagnosetechnik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 40698, 'name': 'Seminar Software and Embedded Systems Engineering', 'version': 6, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Seminar Software Engineering of Embedded Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 2453