'Detection and Estimation', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Applications of statistical inference', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331600 FG Theoretische Grundlagen der Kommunikationstechnik', 'module_description': 'Students acquire the fundamental background on Statistical Inference, including hypothesis testing, signal detection, parameter estimation, and optimal MMSE linear filtering (in particular, Wiener and Kalman filters). This is one of the foundations of modern Electrical Engineering in the ``Systems’ areas such as Automatic Controls, Communications, and Signal Processing.\nHypothesis Testing (maximum a-posteriori probability, Neyman-Pearson testing, minimax testing)\nSignal Detection: uncoded modulation, coded modulation, ISI channels, Viterbi Algorithm, BCJR algorithm\nParameter estimation: Fisher information and Cramer-Rao Bound, minimum variance unbiased estimation, Maximum-Likelihood estimation, Least-Squares, Bayesian estimation\nBayesian inference, sum-product algorithm, and belief propagation\nThe Approximated Message Passing (AMP) algorithm\nWiener filters and Kalman filters', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Foundations of Statistical Inference, Detection, and Estimation', 'group': '34331600 FG Theoretische Grundlagen der Kommunikationstechnik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41106, 'name': 'Projektorientierte App- und Web-Entwicklung', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Projektorientierte App- und Web-Entwicklung', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34335700 FG S-Professur Service Centric Networking (SNET)', 'module_description': 'In der Projektwerkstatt sollen die folgenden Kompetenzen in der methodischen sowie inhaltlichen Bearbeitung von Apps / Web-Apps vermittelt werden:\n\n• Planen und Konzeptionieren von softwarebasierten Lösungen für studentische Alltagsprobleme\n• Grundlagen modernen Projektmanagements (insbesondere agile Projektentwicklung mittels SCRUM)\n• Verwendung von Kanban-Boards\n• Grundlagen des Benutzeroberflächen-Designs („Best Practices“ des App-Designs)\n• Aufbau von Kompetenzen in der Programmierung (Schwerpunktthema)\n• Softwarebasierte Implementation der eigenen Konzeptideen\n• Selbständiges Lösen einfacher informatischer Probleme\n• Regelmäßige Analyse und Bewertung des aktuellen Fortschrittes im Projekt, Selbstreflektion in Bezug auf den jeweils aktuellen Fortschritt und die noch bevorstehenden Herausforderungen\nDie Teilnehmenden sollen im Rahmen des Moduls mehrere eigene App-Ideen praktisch umsetzen. Dabei erlangen sie Kompetenzen in den folgenden Bereichen der App-Entwicklung:\n\nKonzeptionierung von (Web-) Apps:\n• Ideenfindung für Apps / Web-Apps\n• Erarbeitung vollständiger Software-Konzepte aus einer Idee\n\nEinführung in Benutzeroberflächen-Design:\n• Erwerb von Grundkenntnissen des Benutzeroberflächen-Designs\n• Best-Practices im UI- und UX-Design\n• Arbeit mit Design-Software\n• Gestalterische Ausarbeitung des eigenen (Web-) App-Konzeptes\n\nProgrammierung von (Web-) Apps (Schwerpunktthema):\n• Aufbau von Kompetenzen in der Programmierung und Benutzung von Frond-End-Frameworks\n• Selbstständiges Lösen einfacher informatischer Probleme\n• Softwarebasierte Implementation des eigenen (Web-) App-Konzeptes', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Projektorientierte App- und Web-Entwicklung', 'group': '34335700 FG S-Professur Service Centric Networking (SNET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41109, 'name': 'Selected Topics in Natural Language Processing', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Selected topics in natural language processing', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'module_description': "In this seminar, students will learn about selected research topics in natural language processing and its applications. In addition, an introduction to reading scientific papers, learning how to give a good presentation, and how to write a technical report.\n\nDuring the seminar, students will learn:\n- to read and examine the scientific literature critically,\n- to identify and present examples of relevant real-world application fields of the scientific publication,\n- to give a good scientific presentation to peers that is precise, informative, and engaging,\n- to summarize and write a concise technical report including a critical discussion of the research paper (with additional literature research).\nThis seminar discusses selected topics in natural language processing, such as sentiment analysis, named entity recognition, topic modeling, question answering, dialogue systems, machine translation, and natural language generation.\n\nAt the beginning of the seminar, students will learn about how to read and interpret scientific papers, and how to give a good presentation. Every student will be assigned a research paper from a selection of scientific papers. Students' task will be to read the paper, interpret its results and write a technical report of the paper and discuss the topics main application fields. Students will then prepare a presentation and discuss the paper's main outcomes, the critical points, and the main application areas of the scientific paper.", 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Selected Topics in Natural Language Processing', 'group': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41110, 'name': 'Machine Learning and Communications', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Machine Learning and Communications', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'paper', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352800 FG Maschinelles Lernen und Kommunikation', 'module_description': 'Participants of this seminar will acquire knowledge on methodologies used in current AI and communications research. In particular, this seminar course will provide students on the one hand an in-depth theoretical and practical knowledge on topics such as federated machine learning, complexity-reduced machine learning as well as machine learning in changing environments; and on the other hand a know-how in one or more domains of applications in communications. In addition, students will learn how to critically analyze and understand scientific literature and to give effective scientific presentations.\nTopics and methods of new publications on topics related to ML and communications are discussed:\n- Federated machine learning\n- ML with reduced complexity (efficient neural architectures, neural architecture search, NN compression)\n- Machine learning in non-stationary environments\n- Applications of ML in communications applications (video coding, wireless communications, connected devices etc.)\n- Related topics such as privacy, robustness, explainability\n\nStudents present publications (reading club style), explain their structure, methods used, and identify the relation to previous work.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Machine Learning and Communications', 'group': '34352800 FG Maschinelles Lernen und Kommunikation', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41111, 'name': 'State Estimation and Diagnosis of Battery Systems', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'State Estimation and Diagnosis of Battery Systems', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Automotive Systems (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24775}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34312100 FG Elektrische Energiespeichertechnik (EET)', 'module_description': 'The students know about typical measurement techniques applied to battery cells. They can classify and implement state-of-the-art state estimation algorithms for lithium-ion batteries and obtain a deep understanding of states and their importance in lithium-ion batteries. They know the dependencies between states and measurable quantities and can distinguish between diagnosis and prognosis.\nMeasurement methods and quantities: Time domain, frequency domain, test design/checkups\nModels: Discrete equivalent circuit model, single particle model (briefly)\nState definitions and dependencies: State of charge, state of health, state of function, remaining useful life\nState estimation methods: Direct, model-based, data-driven\nDiagnosis and prognosis', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'State Estimation and Diagnosis of Battery Systems', 'group': '34312100 FG Elektrische Energiespeichertechnik (EET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 41112, 'name': 'Data Integration and Large-scale Analysis', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Data Integration and Large-scale Analysis', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Data Integration and Large-scale Analysis', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'module_description': 'Common data and system characteristics include heterogeneous data sources and formats, often in different representations and with data quality issues (which require integration and cleaning), as well as large data collections (which require distributed data storage and analysis). Accordingly, the goals of this module are to convey a basic understanding and practical applicability of\nO1 Major data integration architectures\nO2 Key techniques for data integration and cleaning\nO3 Methods for large-scale data storage and analysis\nThis course covers major data integration architectures, key techniques for data integration and cleaning, as well as methods for large-scale, i.e., distributed, data storage and analysis. In detail, the module covers the following topics which also reflect the lecture calendar (with a separate 90-120min lecture per topic):\n\nA: Data Integration and Preparation\n 01 Introduction and Overview\n 02 Data Warehousing, ETL, and SQL/OLAP\n 03 Message-oriented Middleware, EAI, and Replication\n 04 Schema Matching and Mapping\n 05 Entity Linking and Deduplication\n 06 Data Cleaning and Data Fusion\n 07 Data Provenance (and Blockchain)\n\nB: Large-Scale Data Management and Analysis\n 08 Cloud Computing Fundamentals\n 09 Cloud Resource Management and Scheduling\n 10 Distributed Data Storage\n 11 Distributed, Data-Parallel Computation\n 12 Distributed Stream Processing\n 13 Distributed Machine Learning Systems\n\nThe module contains both lectures and exercises/programming projects which are offered as separate courses in order to increase flexibility.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Data Integration and Large-scale Analysis', 'group': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41113, 'name': 'Uncertainty in Machine Learning', 'version': 3, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Uncertainty in Machine Learning', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352700 FG S-Professur Unsicherheit, inverse Modellierung und maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Knowledge: Students have obtained an extensive overview of the manifold aspects of uncertainty in machine learning, with individual deep insights into a topic of choice.\n\nSkills: Students have acquired or refined skills to independently review and systematically structure scientific literature and have gained experience in presenting their literature research to a critical audience as well as in participating in scientific discussions.\n\nCompetencies: Students are able to critically reflect on novel scientific results in the scope of uncertainty in machine learning. They are able to relate these results to the literature and assess their quality and impact based on adequate metrics.\nMetrology in data science and machine learning\n\nFundamental topics in stochastics, probability theory, and statistics\n- Random variables, probability spaces, probability density functions\n- Independence, marginalization\n- Law of large numbers\n- Central limit theorem\n- Bayesian inference, priors and posteriors \n- Confidence and credibility intervals\n- Bootstrap, Jackknife, method of surrogate data\n\nUncertainty propagation through fixed measurement equations\n- Guide to the Expression of Uncertainty in Measurement (GUM) \n- Polynomial chaos\n- Monte Carlo methods\n\nUncertainty estimation in Machine Learning and Deep Learning\n- Aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty\n- Hierarchical and empirical Bayesian models, predictive distribution\n- Gaussian processes\n- Errors-in-variables models\n- Robust regression\n- Bayesian/Probabilistic Neural Networks\n- Dropout\n- Ensemble Methods\n- Monte Carlo methods\n- Conformal prediction\n- Variational inference\n- Normalizing flows, invertible neural networks, diffusion models\n\nMetrics of Uncertainty Calibration\n- Proper Scoring Rules\n- Calibration Curves\n\nAdvanced Topics\n- Out-of-distribution detection\n- Active learning for uncertainty reduction\n\nApplications of uncertainty estimation in machine learning', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Uncertainty in Machine Learning', 'group': '34352700 FG S-Professur Unsicherheit, inverse Modellierung und maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41114, 'name': 'Topics in Biomedical Data Science', 'version': 3, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Topics in Biomedical Data Science', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352700 FG S-Professur Unsicherheit, inverse Modellierung und maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Knowledge: \nStudents will have an in-depth understanding of biomedical concepts and terminologies used in healthcare and medical research, of the principles and latest developments in machine learning and deep learning, and of how machine learning methods can be applied to biomedical data analysis. Students will become familiar with different types of data sources such as electronic health records, genomic data and imaging data used in biomedical research and their strengths and limitations. Furthermore, students are familiar with the principles underlying statistical inference and causal inference in medical research through this course.\n\nSkills:\nStudents will learn how to effectively communicate findings and insights from biomedical publications. They will also acquire or refine skills to independently review and systematically structure the literature of a well circumscribed field in order to address a given set of questions, and will gain experience in presenting the outcome to a critical audience as well as in participating in scientific discussions. \n\nCompetencies:\nStudents will develop the ability to design machine learning pipelines for analyzing biomedical data. Students will learn how to use various data science tools and techniques to extract insights from biomedical data, including data preprocessing, feature selection, and data visualization. Students will develop critical thinking skills to evaluate the quality of data and the appropriateness of machine learning methods used for specific medical problems. They will learn how to design experiments, interpret results, and draw conclusions from data-driven analyses. Students will also be able to judge the ethical and legal requirements for and ramifications of the use of machine learning in medical science with respect to aspects such as data privacy, informed consent, and bias in algorithms.\nPlanned topics to be covered include:\n- Introduction to data science in biomedical sciences\n- Data processing and cleaning\n- Selected problems in biomedical image analysis\n- Selected problems in the analysis of genomic and other OMICS as well as molecular data\n- Natural language processing (NLP) and selected application in biomedical research\n- Causal Machine learning\n- Clinical decision support systems\n- Precision medicine and personalized healthcare\n- Data privacy and security in biomedical research \n- Bias and fairness in ML models for biomedical research\n- Emerging trends and technologies in biomedical data science', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Topics in Biomedical Data Science', 'group': '34352700 FG S-Professur Unsicherheit, inverse Modellierung und maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41116, 'name': 'Intelligent Security Lab', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Intelligent Security Lab', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353000 FG Maschinelles Lernen und IT-Sicherheit', 'module_description': 'The students acquire knowledge and skills in developing intelligent security systems. These systems use machine learning to analyze and detect security threats. After completion of the module, the student are able to select and apply techniques for data preprocessing and feature extraction on security data. They can compare, apply and evaluate learning algorithms for different security tasks. They know how experimental evaluations are designed and conducted. Finally, they are aware of potential ethical risks of intelligent security systems and critically reflect on their role in society and policy.\nThe lab is a hands-on course that explores the development and evaluation of intelligent security systems. The lab introduces relevant strategies and methods for combining machine learning and security. This includes designing feature spaces and embeddings, selecting learning concepts, applying learning algorithms to security data, and conducting experimental evaluations. The considered security tasks may include \n\n- Attack detection in different data formats\n- Malware analysis and detection\n- Privacy analysis using machine learning\n- Detection of adversarial machine learning\n\nAs security threats regularly change, the specific tasks will be selected and announced individually in each semester.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Intelligent Security Lab', 'group': '34353000 FG Maschinelles Lernen und IT-Sicherheit', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41117, 'name': 'Adversarial Machine Learning', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Adversarial Machine Learning', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353000 FG Maschinelles Lernen und IT-Sicherheit', 'module_description': 'After completion of the module, the students have a comprehensive understanding of attacks and defenses in machine learning. They are able to define security goals, formalize threats and identify vulnerabilities in the application of learning algorithms. They know the working principles of attack types and can transfer them to new domains. These attack types include adversarial examples, poisoning, backdoors, as well as inference attacks. They can apply defense mechanisms, such as adversarial training, certified robustness and attack detection. Finally, students are aware of the ethical implications of adversarial machine learning and understand its impact on society and policy.\nThe lecture covers classic and recent topics in adversarial machine learning. These topics include\n\n- White-box and black-box threat models \n- Techniques for crafting adversarial examples\n- Poisoning and backdoor attacks\n- Membership inference and model extraction\n- Problem-space attacks and attacks in structured domains\n- Adversarial preprocessing \n- Countermeasures measures and defenses\n- Attack and backdoor detection methods\n- Experimental design principles', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Adversarial Machine Learning', 'group': '34353000 FG Maschinelles Lernen und IT-Sicherheit', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41118, 'name': 'Neurokolloquium', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Neurokolloquium', 'type': 'KO', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'module_description': 'Training in current research topics in computational cognitive neuroscience.\nEvery week, relevant papers and/or research results are prepared, presented, and discussed. Students will learn to discuss current research topics in the field of computational cognitive neuroscience with a focus on language and communication in biological and artificial systems.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Neurokolloquium', 'group': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41119, 'name': 'Foundations of Data Literacy and Data Science', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Foundations of Data Literacy and Data Science', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Foundations of Data Literacy and Data Science', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24545}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'module_description': '- Understanding the basic concepts of data, including data type and data structures, and real-world data sources\n- Learning the concepts and skills in computer programming and statistical inference\n- Identifying and retrieving relevant information from data, analyzing and interpreting using statistical methods and visualization techniques, critically evaluating results\n- Ethical considerations and privacy in data handling\nDigitalization and growing amounts of data in science and business require combining skills from different disciplines to create solutions for real-world applications successfully. Therefore, the ability to handle data effectively and critically, and to apply the necessary methodological resources to make informed decisions has become increasingly important across all study fields.\n\nThe goal of this course is to provide, a critical understanding of data, foundational knowledge in statistical methods and visualization techniques to retrieve, understand, and meaningfully use data to make inferences. \n\nStudents will learn to analyze, understand, and interpret data using real-world examples. They will gain skills in data-centric programming using the programming language Python and apply statistical methods to make inferences. In addition, students will learn best practice approaches to data retrieval, preparation, and processing, as well as formulating relevant questions to domain-specific datasets. Finally, the ethical and social considerations of data literacy and data science will be discussed.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Foundations of Data Literacy and Data Science', 'group': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41120, 'name': 'Projekt Funksysteme', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Funksysteme', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien', 'group_str': '34321200 FG Hochfrequenzsysteme', 'module_description': 'Die Funktechnik ist ein wirtschaftlich bedeutendes und stark wachsendes Gebiet der Elektrotechnik mit zahlreichen Bezügen zur Informationstechnik und Informatik. Sie ermöglicht die Übertragung von Daten im Rahmen der drahtlosen Kommunikation, wird zur Erfassung der Umgebung durch Sensorik, Ortung und bildgebende Verfahren eingesetzt und erlaubt die Bestimmung der eigenen Position. Diese Möglichkeiten resultieren in zahlreichen Anwendungen wie Mobilfunk, WLAN, Radar, GPS und Personenscannern in Flughäfen. \n\nDas Ziel dieses Projektes ist es, ein grundlegendes Verständnis von Funksignalen und von den analogen und digitalen Funktionsblöcken von Funksystemen zu gewinnen sowie praktische Erfahrungen mit der Funktechnik im Rahmen von angeleiteten und selbst gestalteten Laborexperimenten zu sammeln. Wie die aktuelle Diskussion um den Mobilfunk der 6. Generation zeigt, werden die verschiedenen Anwendungen der Funktechnik zunehmend verschmelzen und durch interdisziplinäre Methoden wie z.B. des maschinellen Lernens und der künstlichen Intelligenz ergänzt werden, so dass die Lernergebnisse dieses Schwerpunktprojekts für viele Bereiche der Ingenieurswissenschaften und Informatik von Bedeutung sind.\nDie Lehrinhalte des Projekts gliedern sich in Theorieteil, Praxisteil und Projektarbeit:\n\nTheorieteil:\n• Einführung in Signale und Systemkomponenten (Hardware und Software) der Funktechnik, Beschreibung und Modellierung der Signale und Systeme\n• Architekturen und Implementierungskonzepte von Funksystemen, wesentliche Funktionsblöcke\n• Kenngrößen zur Modellierung von Funksystemen\n• Einführung in die Signalverarbeitung mit Matlab\n• Einführung in die Labormesstechnik (Signalerzeugung, Signalanalyse, Netzwerkanalyse (S21))\n\nIm Praxisteil wird die komplette Signalkette eines Funksystems experimentell aufgebaut:\n• Signalerzeugung\n• Übertragungskanal (Funkteile, Antennen, Funkkanal)\n• Signalempfänger\n\nIm Rahmen der Projektarbeit erfolgt eine vertiefende Betrachtung einzelner Komponenten der Signalkette und es werden spezifische Funkübertragungsexperimente durchgeführt. Die Themen der Projektarbeit werden in Abstimmung zwischen Betreuern und den Studierenden festgelegt.\n\nDie genaue Ausgestaltung der Projektarbeit ist auch optional nach individueller Absprache möglich.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Projekt Funksysteme', 'group': '34321200 FG Hochfrequenzsysteme', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien'}, {'id': 41121, 'name': 'Grundlagen der automatischen Spracherkennung', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Automatische Spracherkennung', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Automatische Spracherkennung', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34311900 FG Elektronische Systeme der Medizintechnik', 'module_description': 'Die Teilnehmer verstehen die theoretischen und praktischen Grundlagen automatischer Spracherkennungssysteme. Sie sind in der Lage, die Kernalgorithmen eines einfachen Spracherkenners selbstständig zu implementieren und verstehen die Prinzipien von aktuellen Erkennungssystemen für kleines und großes Vokabular. Dadurch sind sie auch in der Lage, Prinzipien der automatischen Mustererkennungsverfahren für ein breites Anwendungsfeld zu erkennen und kreativ auf neue, verwandte Aufgabenstellungen anzuwenden.\nIn der Vorlesung werden zunächst physiologische und linguistische Grundlagen dargestellt. Es schließt sich eine Einführung in die benötigten mathematischen Grundlagen der Statistik und deren Umsetzung in der Bayes’schen Klassifikation an. Schließlich wird die Anwendung der vorgestellten Methoden zur Klassifikation von Zeitreihen auf das Problem der maschinellen Spracherkennung vorgestellt, wobei tiefe neuronale Netze und deren Einsatz zur Einzelworterkennung und zur Erkennung fließender Sprache einen Schwerpunkt darstellt. Ein Gastvortrag aus der Industrie verstärkt den Praxisbezug. \n\nInnerhalb der Rechnerübung wird in einer aufeinander aufbauenden Reihe von Programmierübungen in Gruppenarbeit ein Spracherkenner für fließend gesprochene Ziffernketten auf der Grundlage von tiefen neuronalen Netzen in einer Encoder-Decoder-Architektur erstellt. Alle dazu benötigten Module, von der Merkmalsextraktion bis zur Ausgabe und Evaluation der Ergebnisse, werden dafür eigenständig in den Gruppen von zwei bis vier Studierenden implementiert.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Grundlagen der automatischen Spracherkennung', 'group': '34311900 FG Elektronische Systeme der Medizintechnik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 41122, 'name': 'Scalable Software Systems Project', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Scalable Software Systems Project', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'k.A.'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361700 FG Scalable Software-Systems', 'module_description': 'Students have acquired detailed insights on research processes in the context of scalable software systems, they have gained hands-on experience in building software prototypes, running experiments, and evaluating and assessing measurement results.\nStudents work in small teams or alone (depending on the concrete topic and its scope) on current research questions in the field of scalable software systems using state-of-the-art technology. Each project will involve several tasks of literature review, coding, benchmarking experiments in the cloud and on edge hardware, data analysis, etc.\n\nDetails depend on the specific project topic and will be announced at the start of the semester.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Scalable Software Systems Project', 'group': '34361700 FG Scalable Software-Systems', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 41124, 'name': 'Websecurity', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Websecurity', 'type': 'UE', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Websecurity', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden erlangen ein umfangreiches Wissen über die häufigsten Schwachstellen in Webanwendungen. Sie sind in der Lage, diverse Klassen von Sicherheitslücken aufzulisten und die jeweiligen Eigenschaften zu unterscheiden. Im Rahmen der integrierten Veranstaltung entwickeln die Studierenden praktische Angriffe gegen die Schwachstellen und können Möglichkeiten zur Behebung daraus ableiten. Darüber hinaus können die Studierenden die Sicherheit von Quelltexten in Bezug auf die gelehrten Schwachstellen beurteilen. Die vermittelten Inhalte haben das Ziel, den Studierenden ein solides Grundwissen und praktischen Umgang mit Webschwachstellen zu vermitteln, sodass diese in der Praxis erkannt und proaktiv vermieden werden können.\nDie Lerninhalte des Moduls orientieren sich an der OWASP Top 10 und sollen theoretische sowie praktische Kenntnisse über gängige Webschwachstellen vermitteln. Zunächst werden wichtige Grundlagen und Konzepte (u.a. HTTP, SOP, Security-Header, SSL/TLS) der Websicherheit gelehrt. Der Fokus liegt auf einer Auswahl der häufigsten clientseitigen (u.a. XSS, CSRF) und serverseitigen (u.a. SQL Injection, Command Injection) Schwachstellen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Websecurity', 'group': '34355100 FG S-Professur Security in Telecommunications', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41126, 'name': 'Algorithms for Networked Systems', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Algorithms for Networked Systems', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'module_description': "Most modern computer systems are inherently distributed and networked, including wireless sensorsystems, datacenters, peer-to-peer systems, or cryptocurrencies, to just give some examples. In order to operate correctly and efficiently, all these systems rely on clever algorithms. Some of the underlying algorithms are fundamental and are used by most of the systems, others are specialized and exploit specific features of the particular distributed system. \n\nThe goal of the module is to provide the students with tools and techniques to reason about efficient algorithms for networks. \n\nThe lecture is problem-oriented and structured around fundamental networking aspects (such as routing, forwarding medium access, etc.) of different networks (e.g., Internet, wireless, cryptocurrency networks, overlay networks, etc.). Each lecture will cover a different fundamental principle (such as use of randomization or indirection) and will be self-contained. \n\nBy the end of the lecture, the student will be able to develop her/his own network algorithms, and formally prove correctness as well as complexity guarantees (e.g., on the computational complexity or the communication complexity). \n\nThe students will also have a good understanding of when to apply which principle, i.e., where randomization can be useful and where not, or to which extent a protocol should be decentralized. The students will further have a good idea of the different natures of today's networked systems. If time permits, we will also extend our discussion beyond computer networks and have an algorithmic look at social networks. \n\nThis module is principally designed to impart: technical skills: 40x, method skills: 40x, system skills 10x, social skills 10x\nThe lectures revolve around fundamental problems and design principles. A tentative outline of the main topics to be covered in the course are \n\n* Network Models for Datacenter Networks, Sensor Networks, Wireless Networks, Mobile Networks etc.\n* Robust Network Topology Design: Self-Stabilizing and Self-Optimizing Networks \n* Randomization: why and how? Basic Tools \n* Algorithms: Local Algorithms, Random Algorithms, Online Algorithms, Dynamic Programming \n* Algorithms for Wireless Medium Access \n* Resource Allocation and Embedding (e.g., energy, bandwidth, CPU) \n* Flow & Congestion Control, Routing \n* Theory of Border Gateway Protocols\n* Algorithms for Cryptocurrency Networks\n* TOR \n* Social Networks: An Algorithmic Perspective", 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Algorithms for Networked Systems', 'group': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41127, 'name': 'Algorithms for Distributed Systems', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Algorithms for Distributed Systems', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24547}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (BSc) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24548}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'module_description': 'Most modern computer systems are inherently distributed and networked, including multi-core computers, machine-learning clusters, wireless sensorsystems, datacenters, peer-to-peer systems, blockchain or cryptocurrencies, to just give some examples. In order to operate correctly and efficiently, all these systems rely on clever algorithms. Some of the underlying algorithms are fundamentaland are used by most of the systems, others are specialized and exploit specific features of the particular distributed system. \n\nThe goal of the module is to provide the students with tools and techniques to reason about efficient algorithms for distributed systems. \n\nThe lecture is problem-oriented and structured into different fundamental principles, such as Distributed Coordination, Decentralization, Randomization, etc. Each lecture will cover a different basic problem (such as Load Balancing, Leader Election, Symmetry Breaking, etc., arising in various different applications, from the Internet over distributed data analytics to sensor networks) and will be self-contained. \n\nBy the end of the lecture, the student will be able to develop her/his own distributed algorithms, and formally prove correctness as well as complexity guarantees (e.g., on the computational complexity or the communication complexity). \n\nThe students will also have a good understanding of when to apply which principle, i.e., where randomization can be useful and where not, or to which extent a distributed system should be decentralized. The students will further have a good idea of the different natures of today\'s distributed systems. If time permits, we will also extend our discussion beyond computer systems and have an algorithmic look at social and biological networks. \n\nThis module is principally designed to impart: \ntechnical skills: 40x, method skills: 40x, system skills 10x, social skills 10x\nThe lectures revolve around fundamental problems and design principles. A tentative outline of the main topics to be covered in the course are \n\n* Models for Distributed Systems: from shared-memory over datacenter applications to Internet-scale systems \n* Algorithmic techniques for small ("shared memory") and large distributed systems ("distributed graph algorithms") \n* Decentralization: why and how? Complexity Measures \n* Randomization: why and how? Basic Tools \n* Algorithms: Local Algorithms, Random Algorithms, Online Algorithms, Dynamic Programming \n* Distributed Algorithms for Leader Election, Coloring, Maximal Independent Sets, Medium Access \n* Resource Allocation and Embedding (e.g., energy, bandwidth, CPU) \n* Social and Biological Networks: An Algorithmic Perspective', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Algorithms for Distributed Systems', 'group': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41128, 'name': 'Advanced Topics in Networked and Distributed Systems', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Topics in Networked and Distributed Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'module_description': 'The successful completion of the seminar module enables the participants to understand recent, complex, and professional literature and to summarize the work. Furthermore, every participant acquires profound knowledge in his/her small topic.\n\nThe goal is to get an understanding of the fundamental theoretical and algorithmic aspects of distributed and networked systems, and their applicability in state-of-the-art and emerging technology. You will learn techniques to model, analyze and optimize networked and distributed systems, and get an understanding of emerging trends and applications.\nGiven the popularity of data-driven applications (e.g., related to business, health and entertainment) and artificialintelligence, computing systems are becoming increasingly distributed and networked. This results in increasingly stringent performance and dependability requirements on such systems. In the seminar, we discuss emerging and innovative new approaches to improve the efficiency and security of distributed and networked systems. We will revisit the theoretical foundations of networked and distributed systems, the underlying fundamental algorithms and optimizations they rely on, and discuss their applicability in modern networks. We will also discuss recent proposals in the literature which aim to render distributed and networked systems more flexible and secure, and explore further optimization opportunities.\n\nContents:\nThe seminar module revolve around fundamental problems and design principles. A tentative outline of the main topics to becovered in the course are\n* Network algorithms and theory of networking\n* Distributed algorithms and optimization\n* Decentralization and scalability\n* Emerging networking technology and applications, and their impact on models and optimizations', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Advanced Topics in Networked and Distributed Systems', 'group': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41129, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum: Algorithm Engineering', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Programmierpraktikum Algorithm Engineering', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden können:\n- Gemäß gegebener Spezifikation Softwarekomponenten entwerfen und implementieren,\n- Effiziente Algorithmen entwickeln und implementieren,\n- Mit aktuellen Werkzeugen zur Softwareentwicklung und -analyse umgehen,\n- moderne Algorithmenbibliotheken und adäquate Datenstrukturen zur schrittweisen Verbesserung ihrer Implementierung benutzen,\n- Projektergebnisse nach innen und außen präsentieren.\n- Projektarbeit in Gruppen organisieren.\n* Strategien effiziente Algorithmen zu entwickeln für (NP-harte) Optimierungsprobleme,\n* Effiziente Implementierungen und Datenstrukturen,\n* Methodiken Flaschenhälse zu identifizieren (z.B. Profilers and Benchmarks), und durch geeignete Datenstrukturen und algorithmische Techniken Performanz entsprechend zu verbessern,\n* Einblick in Problemmodellierung und Lösungsmethoden wie Suchbaumalgorithmen, Datenreduktionstechniken und Vorverarbeitung, exakte, approximative und heuristische Algorithmen und Strategien basierend auf linearem Programmieren (unter Benutzung von etablierten Solvern),\n* effiziente Algorithmen für NP-harte Probleme sowie andere Probleme,\n* Einsatz von Softwareentwicklungs-Werkzeugen, Software-Design und -Analyse, Implementierung, Dokumentation, Evaluation und Test anhand einer praxisrelevanten Aufgabenstellung.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum: Algorithm Engineering', 'group': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41131, 'name': 'Algorithms for Networked and Distributed Systems', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Topics in Networked and Distributed Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - Kernfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24549}, {'name_degree': 'Informationstechnik (Lehramtsbezogen) (M. Ed.) - Zweitfach StuPO 2016', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24550}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'module_description': 'Most modern computer systems are inherently distributed and networked, including multi-core computers, wireless sensorsystems, datacenters, peer-to-peer systems, or cryptocurrencies, to just give some examples In order to operate correctly and efficiently, all these systems rely on clever algorithms. Some of the underlying algorithms are fundamentaland are used by most of the systems, others are specialized and exploit specific features of the particular distributed system. \n\nThe goal of the module is to provide the students with tools and techniques to reason about efficient algorithms for networks and distributed systems. \nThis module is principally designed to impart: technical skills: 40x, method skills: 40x, system skills 10x, social skills 10x\n\nBy the end of the lecture "Algorithms for Distributed Systems" the student will be able to develop her/his own distributed algorithms, and formally prove correctness as well as complexity guarantees (e.g., on the computational complexity or the communication complexity). \n\nThe students will also have a good understanding of when to apply which principle, i.e., where randomization can be useful and where not, or to which extent a distributed system should be decentralized. The students will further have a good idea of the different natures of today\'s distributed systems. If time permits, we will also extend our discussion beyond computer systems and have an algorithmic look at social and biological networks. \n\nBy the end of the lecture "Algorithms for Networked Systems", the student will be able to develop her/his own network algorithms, and formally prove correctness as well as complexity guarantees (e.g., on the computational complexity or the communication complexity). \n\nThe students will also have a good understanding of when to apply which principle, i.e., where randomization can be useful and where not, or to which extent a protocol should be decentralized. The students will further have a good idea of the different natures of today\'s networked systems. If time permits, we will also extend our discussion beyond computer networks and have an algorithmic look at social networks. \n\nThe goal of the seminar is to get an understanding of the fundamental theoretical and algorithmic aspects of distributed and networked systems, and their applicability in state-of-the-art and emerging technology. You will learn techniques to model, analyze and optimize networked systems, and get an understanding of emerging trends and applications.\nPlease attend one out of the two lectures plus the seminar to complete the module.\n\nLectures with tutorial \n\nLecture "Algorithms for Distributed Systems"\n\nThe lecture "Algorithms for Distributed Systems" is problem-oriented and structured into different fundamental principles, such as Distributed Coordination, Decentralization, Randomization, etc. Each lecture will cover a different basic problem (such as Load Balancing, Leader Election, Symmetry Breaking, etc., arising in various different applications, from the Internet over distributed data analytics to sensor networks) and will be self-contained. \n\nThe lecture revolves around fundamental problems and design principles. A tentative outline of the main topics to be covered in the course are \n* Models for Distributed Systems: from shared-memory over datacenter applications to Internet-scale systems \n* Algorithmic techniques for small ("shared memory") and large distributed systems ("distributed graph algorithms") \n* Decentralization: why and how? Complexity Measures \n* Randomization: why and how? Basic Tools \n* Algorithms: Local Algorithms, Random Algorithms, Online Algorithms, Dynamic Programming \n* Distributed Algorithms for Leader Election, Coloring, Maximal Independent Sets, Medium Access \n* Resource Allocation and Embedding (e.g., energy, bandwidth, CPU) \n* Social and Biological Networks: An Algorithmic Perspective\n\nLecture "Algorithms for Networked Systems"\n\nThe lecture "Algorithms for Networked Systems" is problem-oriented and structured around fundamental networking aspects (such as routing, forwarding medium access, etc.) of different networks (e.g., Internet, wireless, cryptocurrency networks, overlay networks, etc.). Each lecture will cover a different fundamental principle (such as use of randomization or indirection) and will be self-contained. \n\nThe lecture revolves around fundamental problems and design principles. A tentative outline of the main topics to be covered in the course are \n* Network Models for Datacenter Networks, Sensor Networks, Wireless Networks, Mobile Networks etc.\n* Robust Network Topology Design: Self-Stabilizing and Self-Optimizing Networks \n* Randomization: why and how? Basic Tools \n* Algorithms: Local Algorithms, Random Algorithms, Online Algorithms, Dynamic Programming \n* Algorithms for Wireless Medium Access \n* Resource Allocation and Embedding (e.g., energy, bandwidth, CPU) \n* Flow & Congestion Control, Routing \n* Theory of Border Gateway Protocols\n* Algorithms for Cryptocurrency Networks\n* TOR \n* Social Networks: An Algorithmic Perspective\n\nSeminar "Advanced Topics in Networked and Distributed Systems"\n\nGiven the popularity of data-driven applications (e.g., related to business, health and entertainment) and artificialintelligence, computing systems are becoming increasingly distributed and networked. This results in increasingly stringent performance and dependability requirements on such systems. In this seminar, we discuss emerging and innovative new approaches to improve the efficiency and security of distributed and networked systems. We will revisit the theoretical foundations of networked and distributed systems, the underlying fundamental algorithms and optimizations they rely on, and discuss their applicability in modern networks. We will also discuss recent proposals in the literature which aim to render distributed and networked systems more flexible and secure, and explore further optimization opportunities.\n\nContents:\nThe seminar revolves around fundamental problems and design principles. A tentative outline of the main topics to becovered in the course are\n* Network algorithms and theory of networking\n* Distributed algorithms and optimization\n* Decentralization and scalability\n* Emerging networking technology and applications, and their impact on models and optimizations', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Algorithms for Networked and Distributed Systems', 'group': '34331700 FG Intelligent Networks and Management of Distributed Systems (INET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41132, 'name': 'Project Hot Topics in Computer Vision A', 'version': 6, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Hot Topics in Computer Vision A', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Geodesy and Geoinformation Science (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (21.03.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24264}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341600 FG Computer Vision and Remote Sensing', 'module_description': 'Project title: "n.n"\n\nParticipants will gain significant insights into computer vision related problems and solutions. The goal is not to explore the whole field of research completely, but rather to confront the participants with the full complexity of one specific problem and to challenge their own initiative. Therefore, we do not provide a pedagogically gentle introduction of the learners to the scientific area, but we allow insights and participation in research and development.\n\nThe ability of the participants to work in a team shall be improved by this module.\nThe exact contents of this project will be announced in time before the start of the term on ISIS.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Project Hot Topics in Computer Vision A', 'group': '34341600 FG Computer Vision and Remote Sensing', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41133, 'name': 'Project Hot Topics in Computer Vision B', 'version': 4, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Hot Topics in Computer Vision B', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Geodesy and Geoinformation Science (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (21.03.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24264}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341600 FG Computer Vision and Remote Sensing', 'module_description': 'Project title: "n.n"\n\nParticipants will gain significant insights into computer vision related problems and solutions. The goal is not to explore the whole field of research completely, but rather to confront the participants with the full complexity of one specific problem and to challenge their own initiative. Therefore we do not provide a pedagogically gentle introduction of the learners to the scientific area, but we allow insights and participation in research and development.\n\nThe ability of the participants to work in a team shall be improved by this module.\nThe exact contents of this project will be announced in time before the start of the term on ISIS.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Project Hot Topics in Computer Vision B', 'group': '34341600 FG Computer Vision and Remote Sensing', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41134, 'name': 'Responsible Artificial Intelligence', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Responsible Artificial Intelligence I', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Responsible Artificial Intelligence II', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352800 FG Maschinelles Lernen und Kommunikation', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden dieses Moduls erwerben Kenntnisse über die Grenzen moderner Systeme der künstlichen Intelligenz im Hinblick auf Kriterien wie Erklärbarkeit, Robustheit, Vertrauenswürdigkeit und Fairness. Sie werden praktische Anwendungsfälle von KI untersuchen, bei denen diese Grenzen ein großes Problem darstellen, und lernen neu entwickelte Methoden zur Überwindung dieser Grenzen kennen. Am Ende des Moduls werden die Studierenden eine klare Vorstellung davon haben, wo wir derzeit in der KI-Forschung und -Entwicklung stehen und was (methodenseitig) noch getan werden muss, um einen verantwortungsvollen KI-Einsatz in der Zukunft sicherzustellen.\nDer Kurs vermittelt die methodischen Grundlagen der Responsible Artificial Intelligence. Ein großer Schwerpunkt des Kurses wird auf Erklärungsmethoden liegen, also Techniken, die als Brücke zwischen dem Menschen und der Black-Box-KI fungieren, indem sie die Funktionsweise der KI und die Basis für ihre Vorhersagen transparent machen. Der Kurs behandelt verschiedene Arten von Erklärungsmethoden und diskutiert ihre Vor- und Nachteile sowie ihre theoretischen Grundlagen.\nDarüber hinaus behandelt der Kurs verschiedene verantwortungsvolle KI-bezogene Themen wie:\n• Robustheit, Zuverlässigkeit und Generalisierbarkeit maschineller Lernmodelle\n• Privatsphäre schützendes maschinelles Lernen\n• KI-Benchmarking, Auditierung und Zertifizierung\n• Bias und Fairness', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Responsible Artificial Intelligence', 'group': '34352800 FG Maschinelles Lernen und Kommunikation', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41135, 'name': 'ROC Foundations for Graduate Research in Data Management and Machine Learning Systems', 'version': 5, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'ROC-PRO Project on the Foundations for Graduate Research in Data Management and Machine Learning Systems', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'ROC-SEM Seminar on the Foundations for Graduate Research in Data Management and Machine Learning Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'module_description': 'Big Data and Machine Learning are key drivers underlying the current wave of innovation in artificial intelligence and data science. Indeed, these drivers have had a profound impact on both the economy and the sciences. \n\nThis course targets research-oriented students who aim to pursue a PhD in Big Data Management -or- Data Science and Engineering Systems/Technologies. Upon completion of this course, students will have learned about contemporary research methodology, including scientific reading, writing, presenting, prototyping and experimental design, gained both theoretical and practical skills in data management and big data technologies, and be attuned to today’s major research challenges in scalable data management and processing. The course is designed to principally impart technical skills (20%), method skills (40%), systems skills (20%), and social skills (20%).\nThe central focus of this module is on contemporary research methodology (CRM), data management technologies, and current research challenges. After an initial presentation on CRM, including scientific reading, writing, presenting, prototyping and experimental design, in subsequent lectures, students will read about foundational data management methods/ technologies and offer a presentation, which will then be followed by an instructor led presentation addressing related advanced topics. \n\nTopics of discussion, include data storage and indexing, specification and compilation of data analysis programs, query optimization and self-tuning, adaptive methods, processing data science pipelines as well as responsible data management. In an accompanying lab component, students will prototype and evaluate discussed methods, technologies, and settings in a methodical and scientific way, and produce a scientific report on their findings.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'ROC Foundations for Graduate Research in Data Management and Machine Learning Systems', 'group': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41136, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum: Datensysteme', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Programmierpraktikum: Datensysteme', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'module_description': 'Studierende des Moduls...\n* haben Methoden der Softwaretechnik praktisch anhand einer komplexen Aufgabenstellung erprobt,\n* haben Teamerfahrungen gesammelt und ihre Teamfähigkeiten verbessert,\n* haben Methoden der effizienten Implementierung ausgewählter Komponenten von Datenbanksystemen kennengelernt und damit tiefere Einblicke erlangt.\nZu Beginn jedes Semesters wird ein neues Projekt (oder mehrere) im Kontext der Implementierung von Datenbanksystemen (z.B., Indexstrukturen, Operatoren wie Joins oder Aggregationen, Bufferpool mit Seitenverdrängung) definiert. Die Studierenden erhalten die API dieser Komponente sowie ausgewählte Benchmarks, und die Aufgabe ist es in selbstorganisierten Teams von 4 Personen korrekte Implementierungen in C, C++, oder Java zu erstellen. Neben der Protypenentwicklung sind auch der systematische Umgang mit Versionsverwaltung, testgetriebener Entwicklung, Entwurfsdokumentation, sowie Laufzeitexperimenten und -verbesserungen von großer Bedeutung. Gleichzeitig erlaubt dieses Programmierpraktikum den Umgang mit vertiefenden Methoden der Gebiete Informationssysteme und Datenanalyse sowie Algorithmen und Datenstrukturen. Der Schwerpunkt liegt jedoch auf dem Erlernen des problemorientieren Einsatzes von Programmierkenntnisse zur Lösung konkreter Fragestellungen, nicht die ganzheitliche funktionale Betrachtung der Implementierung von Datenbanksystemen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum: Datensysteme', 'group': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41137, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum Algorithmen für Spiele und Puzzle', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Programmierpraktikum Algorithmen für Spiele und Puzzle', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34355200 FG S-Professur Neurotechnologie', 'module_description': 'Absolventen und Absolventinnen des Moduls ... \n * haben Algorithmen für Spiele oder zur Lösung von Puzzle entwickelt,\n * haben Teamerfahrungen gesammelt, ihre Teamfähigkeiten verbessert und Techniken der Projektorganisation erfolgreich anwendet,\n * haben effiziente Algorithmen entwickelt und sie mit modernen Werkzeugen der Softwareentwicklung implementiert,\n * haben Projektergebnisse nach innen und außen präsentiert,\n * haben die von ihnen entwickelte Software dokumentiert und evaluiert.\nEinsatz von Softwareentwicklungs-, Kommunikations- und Projektmanagement-Werkzeugen, Projektplanung, Software-Design und -Analyse, Implementierung, Dokumentation, Evaluation und Test anhand einer praxisrelevanten Aufgabenstellung', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum Algorithmen für Spiele und Puzzle', 'group': '34355200 FG S-Professur Neurotechnologie', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41138, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum: Quality Data Science', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Uncertainty in Machine Learning (UNIML)', 'type': 'PPK', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352700 FG S-Professur Unsicherheit, inverse Modellierung und maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Knowledge: Students will be familiar with basic concepts of practical software engineering techniques and their applications in scientific software/data science projects. Further, students will know about different quality dimensions of software/machine learning systems and have a clear understanding of technical means for assuring their quality and reproducibility. \n\nSkills: The project will provide students with practical skills to develop and debug data science applications by analyzing data and code. They will know how to read and critically discuss papers related to machine learning, data science, and biomedical and other applications. Moreover, students will know to implement methods from scientific papers and perform basic quality checks to ensure the correctness of the implementations. Specifically, students will acquire experience in basic software engineering techniques such as unit testing, integration testing, and Git version control and rudimentary skills to develop high-quality software systems. \n\nCompetencies: By the end of the software project, students will have developed the ability to implement procedures and tests to decide whether their implemented software will function as intended. Students can systematically structure the literature of a well-circumscribed field and gain experience in presenting the outcome to a critical audience and participating in scientific discussions. Overall, the software project will equip students with a comprehensive set of skills necessary for developing high-quality scientific software and investigating a small and well-circumscribed research question.\nStudents will carry out a software project, where they will collaborate on a software development project replicating a typical scientific data science/software project. The project will cover various topics, such as mathematical/algorithmic problems (especially data science, machine learning, and explainable AI), software design, and engineering aspects including data processing, data analysis, databases, and software architectures. Depending on the group size, we will specify desired features and behavior of the software to be developed. The students use their implemented methods to explore a clearly defined research problem. The project will entail but is not limited to selected topics relevant to applications in biomedicine, e.g., neuroscience or intensive care medicine.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum: Quality Data Science', 'group': '34352700 FG S-Professur Unsicherheit, inverse Modellierung und maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41139, 'name': 'Masterarbeit Medientechnik', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '30', 'parts': [], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': '', 'faculty': '', 'institute': '', 'group_str': '', 'module_description': '', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 30, 'ects_str': '30', 'name_str': 'Masterarbeit Medientechnik', 'group': '', 'institute_str': ''}, {'id': 41140, 'name': 'Machine Learning 1-X', 'version': 4, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Maschinelles Lernen I', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24795}, {'name_degree': 'Biomedizinische Technik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24814}, {'name_degree': 'Computational Engineering Science (Informationstechnik im Maschinenwesen) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018 (17.01.2018)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24859}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'The students are able to independently apply methods from machine learning on new data. This includes methods for classification, regression, dimensionality reduction and clustering. Moreover, the module teaches the mathematical skills (probability theory, optimization theory) needed to extend and theoretical analyze machine learning methods.\nProbability theory, theory of estimation (e.g. Maximum likelihood, EM algorithm)\n\nMethods from Machine Learning: Dimensionality reduction (PCA), Clustering, Supervised learning (e.g. Regression, LDA, SVM, Gaussian processes)\n\nDepending on the elective: more detailed knowledge about specific machine learning problems, programming skills, or mathematical foundations.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Machine Learning 1-X', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41141, 'name': 'Deep Learning 1-X', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Deep Learning 1 - main', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Understanding of the foundations of neural networks and deep learning, including optimization and regularization aspects. Understanding of the most popular deep neural network architectures used in practice (e.g. convolutional neural networks). Ability to implement a neural network using common deep learning frameworks.\nFoundations of neural networks, including the perceptron, multi-layer perceptrons, activation functions, loss functions, error backpropagation, and the questions of optimization and regularization. Common optimization techniques such as SGD, momentum, and RMSProp. Common regularization techniques such as weight decay, dropout, and Lipschitz constraints. Presentation of popular architectures, such as the convolutional neural network, autoencoders, and recurrent neural networks. Introduction to the PyTorch deep learning framework.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Deep Learning 1-X', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41142, 'name': 'Deep Learning 2-X', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Bayesian Learning', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Classical Topics in ML', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Explainable Machine Learning', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Generative Models', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Machine Learning and Data Management Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Machine Learning in the Sciences', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Mathematische Grundlagen für Maschinelles Lernen', 'type': 'KU', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Software engineering practices for scientific software development', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Understanding of advanced techniques of deep learning, including the application of mathematical concepts such as differential equations, group theory and fix-point iteration in neural networks. Understanding of advanced deep neural network architectures used in practice (e.g. GANs, Transformer, normalizing flows, equivariant neural networks). Ability to implement advanced neural networks using common deep learning frameworks.\nAdvanced techniques such as self-attention, equivariant convolutions, deep equilibrium networks, generative adversarial networks, neural differential equations and normalizing flows. Application of machine learning techniques such as self-supervised / autoregressive learning, density estimation, anomaly detection and reinforcement learning in neural networks. Approaches to accelerate and deploy neural network, such as distillation, quantization, and factorization.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Deep Learning 2-X', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41143, 'name': 'Python for Machine Learning', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Python for Machine Learning', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'The students have a deep theoretical understanding of Python programming, which they can apply autonomously using standard programming tools such as Jupyter notebooks and a debugger.\n\nSpecifically, Students understand general principles underlying Python programming, e.g., Python syntax and advanced paradigms of functional and object-oriented programming. They can apply these skills to advanced data science and machine learning tasks. This includes efficiently and compactly implementing complex tensor operations and implementing visualization methods.\nThe module briefly motivates Python by contrasting it to other programming paradigms (e.g., Julia or C). The module introduces Python-specific programming principles, e.g., duck typing or idiomatic constructs (“Pythonic” syntax) such as generator comprehensions. Students implement visualization code primarily using the framework Matplotlib. \n\nThe module teaches the application of the learned programming skills to machine learning (ML) problems, which includes conceptually understanding exemplary ML tasks. For example, the module teaches the implementation of complex tensor operations (often relevant in machine learning) using acceleration frameworks (such as NumPy or PyTorch) that ensure compact syntax and efficient computation.\n\nThe module teaches the use of programming environments such as Jupyter notebooks and tools like debuggers, which can also be used during the exam.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Python for Machine Learning', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41144, 'name': 'Julia for Machine Learning', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Julia for Machine Learning', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24795}, {'name_degree': 'Luft- und Raumfahrttechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24843}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'The students are able to use the Julia programming language to implement and apply machine learning algorithms. They are familiar with common packages in the Julia ecosystem for classical machine learning, deep learning, and data visualizations. Students have a thorough understanding of automatic differentiation and the ways automatic differentiation packages differ in implementation. They are familiar with best practices for Julia development and can write reproducible, unit-tested code.\nIn the first half of the course, students learn fundamentals of the Julia programming language as well as packages in the wider Julia Machine Learning ecosystem:\n- Performant array processing and linear algebra (LinearAlgebra.jl)\n- Working with tabular data and preprocessing features (DataFrames.jl)\n- Creating visualizations and plots (Plots.jl, StatsPlots.jl)\n- Classical Machine Learning algorithms (MLJ.jl)\n- Mathematical fundamentals of automatic differentiation \n- Differences in implementations of automatic differentiation in Julia (ChainRules.jl, Zygote.jl, Enzyme.jl, ForwardDiff.jl, FiniteDifferences.jl)\n- Training Deep Learning models (Flux.jl, MLDatasets.jl)\n- Common development workflows for package development and scientific experiments (PkgTemplates.jl, DrWatson.jl)\n- Best practices for Julia development, profiling, and debugging (Debugger.jl, Infiltrator.jl, ProfileView.jl, Cthulhu.jl)\n\nIn the second half, student work in groups on a small programming project of their choice, learning how to:\n- Structure and develop a package\n- Write package tests\n- Write and host package documentation', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Julia for Machine Learning', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41145, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum Neue Webtechnologien', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Neue Webtechnologien', 'type': 'PPK', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24545}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34335700 FG S-Professur Service Centric Networking (SNET)', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden erhalten einen Überblick über weiterführende Überlegungen bei der Web- und App-Entwicklung, insbesondere in Bezug auf Dateneigentum, Sicherheit und Dezentralisierung. Über gesellschaftliche und ethische Themen hinaus erlernen sie den Umgang mit konkreten Programmierwerkzeugen, die im Speziellen für die Umsetzung vorstehender Aspekte ausgelegt sind.\n\nIm Verlauf des Moduls befassen sich die Studierenden mit\n* der Ideenbildung für Webanwendungen\n* der funktionalen und gestalterischen Konzeption selbiger\n* der technischen Umsetzung eines Anwendungskonzepts\n* der Präsentation und Evaluation eines Projekts\n\nNach Abschluss des Moduls werden die Studierenden befähigt sein, Anwendungsarchitekturen kritisch zu bewerten, Softwareprojekte zu konzipieren und zu realisieren sowie die Programmier-Technologien "UIX" und "DATEX" für die Entwicklung ihrer Anwendungen effizient zu nutzen.\nIm Kontext von Webanwendungen werden Grundüberlegungen zu folgenden Themen diskutiert:\n* Eigentum an personenbezogenen Daten und Privatsphäre\n* SIcherheit, Verschlüsselung und berechtigter Fremdzugriff auf Daten\n\nKonkrete Technologien, die ausdrücklich unter Berücksichtigung dieser Aspekte entwickelt wurden, werden in der Folge eingeführt:\n* "Datex", ein Datentransfer-Protokoll\n* "UIX", ein User-Interface-Framework\n\nIn Gruppen werden die Studierenden Ideen für eine Webanwendung erdenken und diese im Laufe des Semesters gemeinsam zu einem Konzept ausarbeiten und schließlich mittels zuvor eingeführter Technologien umsetzen. Abschließend folgt eine Präsentation und Auswertung der erarbeiteten Anwendung.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum Neue Webtechnologien', 'group': '34335700 FG S-Professur Service Centric Networking (SNET)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41146, 'name': 'Machine Learning and Data Management Systems', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Machine Learning and Data Management Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'paper', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'module_description': 'After the course the students are able to communicate complex subjects in oral presentations and in written form (journal/conference format). The participants have the capabitlity to do literature research and have in depth knowledge of a specific current topic of Machine Learning and Data Management Systems.\nThis is a joint research-oriented seminar of the Machine Learning Group and the Data Management Group. Throughout the seminar, students will have the opportunity to learn about recent advances in the intersection of Machine Learning and Data Management Systems.\n\nExample topics include:\n\n- Federated/Deep Ensemble Learning and Data Management Systems.\n- Carbon-aware data management systems and Machine Learning.\n- Compression of ML Systems.\n- Continual, Lifelong, and Online Learning.\n- Data management systems for Lifelong Learning.\n- Hashing and sketches.\n- Building ML pipelines for large large scale data preparation, model training and model debugging, versioning, and monitoring.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Machine Learning and Data Management Systems', 'group': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41147, 'name': 'Radio Astronomy Project (SIERRA)', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Radio Astronomy', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Luft- und Raumfahrttechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24843}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien', 'group_str': '34321100 FG Hochfrequenztechnik/ Hochfrequenztechnik-Photonik', 'module_description': 'In the scope of a curricular project, the participants are going to build radio astronomy components or perform radio astronomy measurements and data processing within interdisciplinary teams. They will gain basic knowledge in high frequency technology and signal processing as well as electrical, mechanical and software engineering. They will understand the working principles of hardware and software related to radio astronomy. In combination with the knowledge and skills gained in other courses in electrical and computer engineering, the participants will be able to set up a a simple radio telescope. They will document and present their work at the end of the project.\n\nAfter successful completion of this module, students will be able to\n- work in an interdisciplinary project team,\n- understand general structure and components of radio telescopes,\n- organize small interdisciplinary engineering projects,\n- use open source soft- and hardware tools for management and development.\n- Applied technical know-how regarding radio astronomy: e.g. characteristics of electromagnetic waves, components for transmitter and\nreceiver circuits, antennas, transmission path, electronics, mechanics, programming, networking and other IT components etc.\n- Practical hardware, software and/or system design as well as manufacturing and implementation\n- Using electrical and RF measuring instruments and/or troubleshooting tools\n- Methods for planning and organizing projects\n- Technical and project documentation and presentation of the practical work', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Radio Astronomy Project (SIERRA)', 'group': '34321100 FG Hochfrequenztechnik/ Hochfrequenztechnik-Photonik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien'}, {'id': 41148, 'name': 'Machine Learning in Neuroscience', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Machine Learning in Neuroscience', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24795}, {'name_degree': 'Biomedizinische Technik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24814}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'paper', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'The students are familiar with a range of applications of machine learning in neuroscience, and with fruitful interactions between machine learning and neuroscience. They have a thorough understanding of a number of machine learning concepts and can explain how these concepts have been applied in neuroscience. The students have an overview of several research areas in neuroscience and know some examples of neuroscience-inspired machine learning. The students have been exposed to recent research literature and have gained experience in understanding and presenting original research.\nThe course is based on recent publications that apply machine learning to neuroscience or advance machine learning by using inspirations from neuroscience. The course presents these results and provides the necessary background and context both for the machine learning aspect, as well as the neuroscience aspect.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Machine Learning in Neuroscience', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41150, 'name': 'Blockchain Prototyping', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Blockchain Prototyping', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'module_description': 'Students have hands-on experimentation with all aspects of software project work (including team-based software development, project management, collaborative decision making, documenting and communicating project results). They are able to solve real-world problems in the context of the design, implementation, and evaluation of blockchain-based application systems in, e.g., enterprise, start-up, and IoT contexts.\nSmall groups of students analyze and solve challenging software and prototyping problems. They explore and use modern, state-of the art blockchain technologies, e.g., Ethereum, and modern software technology stacks as applicable to the specific project focus defined each term. Depending on the focus, they apply cutting-edge blockchain concepts such as on-off-chain-models, hybrid cloud-blockchain-architectures, or zero-knowledge-proofs. The student teams work independently, supported and supervised by members of the chair.\n\nHands-on experimentation with blockchain-based systems is expected. Concrete tasks and project objectives as well as themes and technology stacks will be communicated at the beginning of the term. Some projects may be in cooperation with external partners.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Blockchain Prototyping', 'group': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 41152, 'name': 'Privacy Prototyping', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Privacy Prototyping', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'module_description': 'Students have hands-on experimentation with all aspects of software project work (including team-based software development, project management, collaborative decision making, documenting and communicating project results). They are able to solve real-world problems in the context of the design, implementation, and evaluation of practically feasible, novel privacy technologies and privacy-friendly enterprise-grade application systems, particularly also covering privacy principles beyond security and anonymity.\nSmall groups of students analyze and solve challenging software and prototyping problems. They explore and use modern and novel approaches to technically materialize privacy principles in real-world distributed software systems. The employ modern software technology stacks as applicable to the specific project focus defined each term. The student teams work independently, supported and supervised by members of the chair.\n\nHands-on experimentation with privacy-enhancing technologies, cloud services and (potentially complex) open source systems is expected. Concrete tasks and project objectives as well as themes and technology stacks will be communicated at the beginning of the term. Some projects may be in cooperation with external partners.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Privacy Prototyping', 'group': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 41153, 'name': 'Advanced Cloud Prototyping', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Cloud Prototyping - Specialisation', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'module_description': 'Students have advanced hands-on experience with all aspects of software project work (including team-based software development, project management, collaborative decision making, documenting and communicating project results). They are able to solve real-world problems in the context of the advanced design, implementation, and evaluation of cloud-based application systems in, e.g., enterprise, start-up, and IoT contexts. They are able to identify and articulate open research questions and theses for further work.\nSmall groups of students analyze and solve challenging software and prototyping problems. They explore and use public cloud services, e.g., Amazon Web Services, and modern software technology stacks as applicable to the specific project focus defined each term. Depending on the focus, they apply advanced cloud concepts, paradigms, and practices such as cloud-native, serverless architectures, and/or quality-driven system development and assessment. The student teams work independently, supported and supervised by members of the chair.\n\nHands-on experimentation with cloud services and open source systems is expected. Concrete tasks and project objectives as well as themes and technology stacks will be communicated at the beginning of the term. Some projects may be in cooperation with external partners.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Advanced Cloud Prototyping', 'group': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 41154, 'name': 'Advanced Blockchain Prototyping', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Blockchain Prototyping - Specialisation', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'module_description': 'Students have advanced hands-on experience with all aspects of software project work (including team-based software development, project management, collaborative decision making, documenting and communicating project results). They are able to solve real-world problems in the context of the advanced design, implementation, and evaluation of blockchain-based application systems in, e.g., enterprise, start-up, and IoT contexts. They are able to identify and articulate open research questions and theses for further work.\nSmall groups of students analyze and solve challenging software and prototyping problems. They explore and use modern, state-of the art blockchain technologies, e.g., Ethereum, and modern software technology stacks as applicable to the specific project focus defined each term. Depending on the focus, they apply advanced cutting-edge blockchain concepts such as on-off-chain-models, hybrid cloud-blockchain-architectures, or zero-knowledge-proofs. The student teams work independently, supported and supervised by members of the chair.\n\nHands-on experimentation with blockchain-based systems is expected. Concrete tasks and project objectives as well as themes and technology stacks will be communicated at the beginning of the term. Some projects may be in cooperation with external partners.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Advanced Blockchain Prototyping', 'group': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 41156, 'name': 'Advanced Privacy Prototyping', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Privacy Prototyping - Specialisation', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'ICT Innovation (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24903}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden', 'group_str': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'module_description': 'Students have advanced hands-on experience with all aspects of software project work (including team-based software development, project management, collaborative decision making, documenting and communicating project results). They are able to solve real-world problems in the context of the advanced design, implementation, and evaluation of practically feasible, novel privacy technologies and privacy-friendly enterprise-grade application systems, particularly also covering privacy principles beyond security and anonymity.\nSmall groups of students analyze and solve challenging software and prototyping problems. They explore and use advanced modern and novel approaches to technically materialize privacy principles in real-world distributed software systems. The employ modern software technology stacks as applicable to the specific project focus defined each term. The student teams work independently, supported and supervised by members of the chair.\n\nHands-on experimentation with privacy-enhancing technologies, cloud services and (potentially complex) open source systems is expected. Concrete tasks and project objectives as well as themes and technology stacks will be communicated at the beginning of the term. Some projects may be in cooperation with external partners.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Advanced Privacy Prototyping', 'group': '34361400 FG Wirtschaftsinformatik - Information Systems Engineering (ISE)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Wirtschaftsinformatik und Quantitative Methoden'}, {'id': 41157, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum Scalable Software Systems', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Programmierpraktikum Scalable Software Systems', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34332700 FG Mobile Cloud Computing', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden erwerben folgende Kenntnisse:\n- Selbstorganisierte Leitung eines Softwareentwicklungsprojekts\n- Nutzung von Projektmanagementtechniken und -werkzeugen\n- Entwicklung einer modernen verteilten Softwareanwendung\n- Präsentation und Dokumentation der Arbeit\nIn diesem Praktikum sollen Methoden und Werkzeuge der Softwaretechnik und des Projektmanagements praktisch bei der selbstorganisierten Entwicklung einer modernen verteilten Anwendung (z.B. Cloud, Edge, IoT, Web) erlernt und vertieft werden. Teil davon sind Planung, Implementierung, Dokumentation und Präsentation der Ergebnisse.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum Scalable Software Systems', 'group': '34332700 FG Mobile Cloud Computing', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41158, 'name': 'Multi-Robot Systems', 'version': 2, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Multi-Robot Systems', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34342300 FG Multi-Roboter-Systeme', 'module_description': 'The students will have a detailed understanding about key challenges and possible algorithmic solutions that arise when coordinating multiple robots:\n• Collision Avoidance, Distributed Control, Relative State Estimation, and Multi-Robot Motion Planning;\n• Task Assignment;\n• Communication Limitations.\n\nStudents will be able to:\n• Decide which algorithm(s) to use for a given target application that involves multiple robots;\n• Effectively read and discuss book chapters and classical seminal papers.\nThe course focuses on applications of multiple robots and robotic swarms, e.g., for inspection, exploration, assembly, or surveillance. Compared to a single robot, new challenges arise in all parts of the robotics pipeline: perception and state estimation (of other robots), decision making (collision avoidance and achieving a common goal), and controls (safety or other guarantees). We consider classic seminal and current book chapters and scientific papers that tackle these challenges both from a theoretical and a practical/application perspective.\n\nConcrete algorithms/topics may include:\n\nApplications/Field Robotics:\n • Monitoring/Environment: Surveillance, Agricultural robotics, Firefighting robots\n • Construction: Assembly Planning\n • Exploration and Mapping (e.g., DARPA Challenges)\n\nDecision Making:\n • Hungarian Method and other assignment algorithms\n • Path and motion planning (CBS, M*)\n • Distributed Optimization (ADMM)\n • Dec-POMDPs\n • Distributed Systems: Lamport Clock, PAXOS, Distributed hash tables\n\nControls:\n • Collision Avoidance (Buffered Voronoi Cells, Control Barrier Functions)\n • Rigidity and Formation Control\n\nPerception/State Estimation:\n • Relative Pose Estimation\n • Multi-Robot SLAM\n • Distributed Kalman Filters', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Multi-Robot Systems', 'group': '34342300 FG Multi-Roboter-Systeme', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41159, 'name': 'Flying Robots', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Flying Robots', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34342300 FG Multi-Roboter-Systeme', 'module_description': 'The students will have a detailed understanding about flying robots (especially multirotors) from a theoretical and practical perspective, including:\n• Underlying physical models and simulation;\n• Nonlinear control;\n• Nonlinear state estimation;\n• Motion planning.\n\nStudents will be able to:\n• Mathematically understand the algorithms used on flying robots;\n• Implement these algorithms in a high-level language (Python);\n• Implement these algorithms in a low-level language (C) such that they run in real-time on a microcontroller (STM32);\n• Operate and tune real flying robots (Bitcraze Crazyflie 2.1); and\n• Use a software-in-the-loop (SITL) engineering approach.\nThe course is largely practical, where students work towards implementing all the components that are needed on a modern flight controller. The different aspects are:\n• Introduction to flying robots (multirotors and variants, fixed-wing, hybrid)\n• Underlying physics models of the dynamics\n• Control approaches (differential flatness, geometric controllers for attitude and position)\n• State estimation techniques (Mahony filter, Extended Kalman filters)\n• Motion planning for flying robots (optimization using splines, search-based methods, sampling-based approaches)\n• Advanced topics may include: \n • Applications for flying robots\n • MPC and nonlinear control techniques\n • Aerodynamic effects such as ground effect and downwash\n • Estimation/planning/control for multi-robot teams\n • Machine learning for flying robots\n\nOn the practical level, students have the following milestones:\n• Physics:\n [Sim] Implementation of a multirotor simulator using Newton-Euler equations\n [Real] Comparing with real-world recorded data\n• Control:\n [Sim] Implementation of a geometric controller\n [Real] Implementation in C, testing using SITL in the simulator and with a real robot using a joystick\n• State Estimation:\n [Sim] Implementation of an EKF fusing IMU and optical flow, tested with real data\n [Real] Implementation in C, testing using SITL, verification on the real robot\n• Motion Planning:\n [Sim] Implementation of an optimization-based motion-planner\n [Real] verification on the real robot', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Flying Robots', 'group': '34342300 FG Multi-Roboter-Systeme', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41160, 'name': 'Computational modeling - A practical course', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Computational modeling - A practical course', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352100 FG Modellierung kognitiver Prozesse', 'module_description': 'Computational models are an important scientific tool that can be applied to a broad variety of problems. In most modelling courses, students primarily learn about existing standard models for a selection of important phenomena. Little emphasis is usually put on the practical skills that are needed to develop new models for new problems, or to adapt existing models to different problems. The goal of the module is to convey these skills. \n\nAfter completion of the course, students will be able to design their own mathematical models. They will know that there are usually many different models for the same problem. They will have practised to single out what is relevant for a given problem at hand. They will know a set of basic building blocks for models, and how they can be combined to translate mechanistic hypotheses into equations. They will have practised to justify their design choices before others, both written and orally. Finally, they will have learned to refine their model based on simulations and mathematical analyses.\n\nThe main focus of the course is on mechanistic models for dynamical systems.\n- What are computational models good for? \n- What characterises a good model? \n- The model development process: \n * Identification of relevant quantities \n * Translation of hypotheses into mathematical equations\n * Model refinement based on simulations and/or mathematical analyses\n- Building blocks for computational models: \n * Linear models\n * Different forms of nonlinearity (attractors, multiplicative and point nonlinearities)\n * Different forms of stochasticity (finite state models with stochastic transitions, Gaussian noise and Langevin equations)\n * Basics of Bayesian models', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Computational modeling - A practical course', 'group': '34352100 FG Modellierung kognitiver Prozesse', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41161, 'name': 'High-Frequency Integrated Systems and Applications', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Integrated high frequency systems and applications', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien', 'group_str': '34322000 FG Integrierte Breitband- und Höchstfrequenzschaltungen', 'module_description': 'This seminar covers the most relevant areas of application of high-frequency integrated circuits: wireless communication systems, optoelectronic systems, radar systems and high-frequency sensor systems.\nAfter successful participation in the seminar, the students will gain understanding of:\n- The architecture of high-frequency systems\n- The most common system-level performance parameters and metrics\n- The role of integrated circuits within high-frequency systems and their impact on the overall performance\n- High speed data communication systems \n- Opto-electronic systems\n- Millimeter wave radar systems\n- High frequency sensors for biomedical applications', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'High-Frequency Integrated Systems and Applications', 'group': '34322000 FG Integrierte Breitband- und Höchstfrequenzschaltungen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien'}, {'id': 41162, 'name': 'Compiling Techniques', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Compiling Techniques', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Compiling Techniques', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353200 FG Programmiersprachen', 'module_description': 'On completion of this course, the student will be able to:\n * understand the design of modern compilers\n * analyse compilation tasks and apply standard compilation techniques\n * design, implement and apply modifications to standard compilation techniques and algorithms\n * implement a fully functional compiler following modern compiler design principles\nIn this course, students learn about the phases of a modern programming language compiler, with an emphasis on techniques widely used in practice. Students will learn about implementing compiler passes in a real compiler framework. The course project will require students to implement a complete compiler from scratch for a simple programming language, targeting a real machine assembly.\n\n* Introduction: structure of a compiler\n* Lexical analysis: tokens, regular expressions, Lex\n* Parsing: context-free grammars, predictive and LR parsing\n* Abstract syntax: semantic actions, abstract parse trees\n* Semantic analysis: symbol tables, bindings, type-checking\n* Intermediate code: intermediate representations, SSA, translations\n* Liveness analysis: solution of dataflow equations\n* Instruction selection: algorithms for selection, RISC and CISC\n* Register allocation: colouring by simplification, coalescing\n* Real assembly language: ARM, MIPS, RISC-V, or similar\n* Advanced Topics may include: automatic parallelisation, popular open-source compilers: GCC, LLVM, MLIR', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Compiling Techniques', 'group': '34353200 FG Programmiersprachen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41163, 'name': 'Programmierpraktikum: Entwurf und Implementierung von Programmiersprachen', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Programming Language Design and Implementation', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353200 FG Programmiersprachen', 'module_description': 'Graduates of this module have knowledge and practical experience in the field of programming language design and implementation. The focus is on software design, programming and implementation of programming languages, e.g. in (domain-specific) compilers, but also IDEs, debuggers and other tools for software development. Project work in a team additionally teaches social and project management skills.\nModern programming languages support software development in challenging application areas and for complex hardware architectures. Advanced type systems help identify problems without executing the software. Compilers (semi-)automatically optimize the software so that it efficiently exploits the hardware. This Programmierpraktikum introduces modern technologies for designing and implementing programming languages.\n\nFor this purpose, a practical task is set, which is to be solved by the students independently in a team using selected technologies. The joint task serves to implement the methods and knowledge acquired in the basic studies of computer science. This takes place under conditions that are as realistic as possible, including planning, implementation, management, coordination and presentation of results of the concrete team task.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Programmierpraktikum: Entwurf und Implementierung von Programmiersprachen', 'group': '34353200 FG Programmiersprachen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41164, 'name': 'Seminar: Aktuelle Forschungsthemen in Programmiersprachen und Compilern', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Current Research Topics in Programming Languages and Compilers', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353200 FG Programmiersprachen', 'module_description': "In this seminar, students will be introduced to advanced topics in programming languages and compilers. Students will learn how to critically read scientific materials drawn from the programming languages, compilers, and related literature.\nStudents will also learn about the core elements of a technical presentation and have an opportunity to sharpen their critical thinking skills. Furthermore, students will learn how to write a technical report.\nDuring the initial weeks, students will be offered lectures on the core elements of a technical presentation, how to offer an effective presentation, how to critically read scientific papers, and how to write a technical report. In addition, each seminar participant will be assigned a scientific topic as well as reading materials (e.g., drawn from a textbook on programming languages theory or compilers). In the subsequent weeks, each student will read their assigned reading materials and study them deeply, in order to assemble and deliver their own presentation. Moreover, each week, students will be required to reflect on the main challenges addressed in each of their peers' presentations.", 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Seminar: Aktuelle Forschungsthemen in Programmiersprachen und Compilern', 'group': '34353200 FG Programmiersprachen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41165, 'name': 'Robot Learning', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Robot Learning', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Automotive Systems (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24775}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34342100 FG Intelligent Systems', 'module_description': 'The students have a systematic understanding of the wide variety of contexts and problems settings in which machine learning methods can be applied within robotics.\nThey understand how the learning problems are mathematically formulated in these settings.\nThey can decide which kinds of learning methods are applicable and appropriate for which kinds of problem settings.\nThey can transfer advances in machine learning to applications in robotics.\nThey have first experience with some basic learning methods applied to robotics problems.\nThe term Robot Learning generally denotes the use of learning methods in the context of robotics, which is ubiquitous in modern robotics research. This course aims to provide a systematic introduction to the field, in particular to the various contexts and problem setting where machine learning can be applied and the specific learning methods themselves. This includes topics such as:\n\n• System identification, model learning, residual model learning\n• Imitation learning, behavior cloning, learning from demonstration\n• Reinforcement Learning (RL), skill learning, offline RL\n• Constraint learning, grasp learning, iterative learning control\n• Learning to predict plans, learning to warmstart MPC or optimization\n• Inverse RL\n• Learning as optimization, in-situ learning/trial-and-error vs. offline optimization\n• Evolutionary learning\n• Online/lifelong learning\n• Safe Learning\n• Multi-robot learning', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Robot Learning', 'group': '34342100 FG Intelligent Systems', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41166, 'name': 'The Software Horror Picture Show', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'The Software Horror Picture Show', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2013', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24397}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24840}, {'name_degree': 'Naturwissenschaften in der Informationsgesellschaft (BSc) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24858}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351900 FG Modelle und Theorie Verteilter Systeme (MTV)', 'module_description': 'Absolventinnen und Absolventen dieses Moduls kennen und verstehen - anhand von einer ausgewählten Menge von Beispielen - die Auswirkungen von Softwarefehlern, die in der Praxis entweder hohe finanzielle Verluste oder gar den Verlust von Menschenleben verursachten. Sie gewinnen Wertschätzung für Qualitätssicherungspraktiken und haben ein höheres Bewusstsein für mögliche Fehler. Die Studierenden sind in der Lage wissenschaftliche Themen vor einem Fachpublikum zu präsentieren und in einem anschließenden Streitgepräch über ihr Thema zu diskutieren. Dabei kennen sie grundlegende und fortgeschrittene Präsentationstechniken um den Inhalt eines Referats möglichst klar und verständlich anzubringen.\nEine Auswahl von Beispielen von mehr oder weniger berühmt gewordenen Softwarefehlern. \nIm jeweiligen Fall Darlegung des Umfelds und der Randbedingungen. \nPräzise (wenn nicht gar formale) Charakterisierung der Fehler und ihrer Auswirkungen. \nAnalyse/Abschätzung, wie die Fehler hätten vermieden werden können.\nDarüber hinaus Diskussion, warum solche Fehler auftreten und wie man generell mit Fehlern effektiver umgehen könnte. \nVerschiedene Techniken zur Präsentation und textuellen Aufbereitung der vorgestellten Themen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'The Software Horror Picture Show', 'group': '34351900 FG Modelle und Theorie Verteilter Systeme (MTV)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41167, 'name': 'Natural Language Processing in Humans and Machines', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Natural Language Processing in Humans and Machines', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24545}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'module_description': "In this seminar, students will learn about selected research topics in natural language processing in humans and machines. In addition, an introduction to cognitive computational neuroscience, reading scientific papers, learning how to give a good presentation, and how to write a technical report.\n\nDuring the seminar, students will learn:\n- to read and examine the scientific literature critically,\n- to identify and present examples of relevant real-world application fields of the scientific publication,\n- to give a good scientific presentation to peers that is precise, informative, and engaging,\n- to summarize and write a concise technical report including a critical discussion of the research paper (with additional literature research)\nThis seminar discusses selected topics in natural language processing in humans and machines in the intersection between computer science and computational cognitive neuroscience. \n\nAt the beginning of the seminar, students will learn about how to read and interpret scientific papers, and how to give a good presentation. Every student will be assigned a research paper from a selection of scientific papers. Students' task will be to read the paper, interpret its results and write a technical report of the paper and discuss the topics main application fields. Students will then prepare a presentation and discuss the paper's main outcomes, the critical points, and the main application areas of the scientific paper.", 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Natural Language Processing in Humans and Machines', 'group': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41168, 'name': 'Data Science for Cognitive Neuroscience', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Data Science for Cognitive Neuroscience', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24545}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'oral', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'module_description': '- Understanding of experiments and data used in cognitive neuroscience research.\n- First hand experience with real brain recorded data, eg. EEG and fMRI.\n- Identifying and retrieving relevant information from brain data and interpreting them using data analysis techniques.\n- Learn how to develop and test a hypothesis.\nThe human brain is an intricate and complex information processing system, giving rise to an exciting interdisciplinary field of research. Understanding how it works is a challenging scientific quest. In recent decades, new brain imaging techniques have allowed us to "see" the brain in action, leading to the growth of cognitive neuroscience. Cognitive neuroscience explores the neural mechanisms that underlie a wide range of cognitive functions, linking brain activity to the tasks it performs. This field fosters exciting collaborations with psychology, biology, physics, and computer science, offering a comprehensive approach to understanding the brain.\n\nIf you are intrigued by the inner workings of the brain and eager to employ cutting-edge brain imaging and data analysis tools for it’s exploration, this course is tailored for you! During this course, you will acquire proficiency in utilizing Python programming for comprehending, manipulating, and exploring human brain recordings (such as ECoG, EEG, MEG, and fMRI). You will also learn how to create and test hypotheses about how the brain processes information using real data. Additionally, you will learn invaluable analysis techniques to make sense of brain recording data.\n\nThis course provides hands-on experience in the data analysis of brain data, enabling you to gain a deep insight into the experiments and data employed in the cognitive neuroscience field. Furthermore, the data analysis techniques and investigative approaches you learn will be readily transferable to research in other disciplines.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Data Science for Cognitive Neuroscience', 'group': '34353100 FG Sprache und Kommunikation in biologischen und künstlichen Systemen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41169, 'name': 'Workshop Machine Learning Foundations for Physicists', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Beginners Workshop Machine Learning', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'This workshop is designed to give students with a background in physics an introduction to the field of machine learning, as well as to introduce them to state-of-the-art research in machine learning methods in physics.\nStudents will have a good overview of machine learning methods applied in physics, such as accelerated simulations of lattice gauge theories, quantum, classical and quantum-inspired machine learning, and computation of generalized parton distributions with learnable denoising approaches.\n- Foundations in Machine Learning: \n -> Classical Methods like Linear Regression and the Perceptron \n -> Unsupervised Learning: Clustering\n -> Bayesian Methods \n -> Introduction Artificial Neural Networks, Deep Learning, Autodiff Frameworks like Pytorch.\n -> Specialized Network architectures, like Recurrent and Convolutional Neural Networks\n -> Geometric Deep Learning\n -> Deep Generative Models, like Normalizing Flows', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Workshop Machine Learning Foundations for Physicists', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41170, 'name': 'Einführung Photovoltaik', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Ausgewählte Kapitel der Photovoltaik', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Photovoltaik - Grundlagen und kristalline Silizium-Solarzellen (PV1)', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien', 'group_str': '34325400 FG S-Professur Photovoltaik', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden besitzen vertiefte Kenntnisse auf dem Gebiet der Erzeugung erneuerbarer Energie mit Hilfe photovoltaischer Systeme. Sie haben ein Verständnis für die grundlegende, physikalische Wirkungsweise von Solarzellen und sind in der Lage die Performance zu analysieren und Strategien zur Optimierung von Solarzellen zu entwickeln. Sie kennen die grundlegenden Verfahren zur Herstellung von Solarzellen und können verschiedene Solarzellkonzepte beschreiben sowie deren Wirkungsweise beurteilen. Nach Abschluss des Moduls haben die Studierenden die grundlegenden Kenntnisse, um sich mit der photovoltaischen Energieerzeugung in Forschung und Praxis zu beschäftigen.\nDas Ziel des Moduls ist es, ein grundlegendes physikalisches Verständnis von Solarzellen bzw. Solarmodulen zu vermitteln. In der Vorlesung werden die grundlegenden physikalischen Prozesse, die bei der photovoltaischen Energiewandlung im Halbleiter ablaufen, generelle Überlegungen zum Wirkungsgrad photovoltaischer Systeme, klassische und moderne Konzepte für kristalline Siliziumsolarzellen sowie der Herstellungsprozess von Solarzellen gelehrt. Das Seminar bietet die Möglichkeit zur Vertiefung der Kenntnisse, z.B. der grundlegenden physikalischen Prozesse, der Analyse photovoltaischer Materialien und Systeme oder der Herstellung von Solarzellen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Einführung Photovoltaik', 'group': '34325400 FG S-Professur Photovoltaik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien'}, {'id': 41171, 'name': 'Vertiefung Photovoltaik', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Photovoltaik - Dünnschichtsolarzellen und neue Konzepte (PV2)', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien', 'group_str': '34321800 FG Perowskit-Solarzellen', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden besitzen vertiefte Kenntnisse auf dem Gebiet der Erzeugung erneuerbarer Energie mit Hilfe photovoltaischer Systeme. Sie haben ein Verständnis für die grundlegende, physikalische Wirkungsweise von Solarzellen und sind in der Lage die Performance zu analysieren und Strategien zur Optimierung von Solarzellen zu entwickeln. Sie kennen die grundlegenden Verfahren zur Herstellung von Solarzellen und können verschiedene Aufbauten beschreiben sowie deren Wirkungsweise beurteilen. Die Studierenden kennen verschiedene Typen von Dünnschichtsolarzellen (z.B. GaAs, CIGS, perovskite, OPV), welche auf verschiedenen Absorbermaterialien basieren. Darüber hinaus haben sie komplexere Solarzellkonzepte wie Tandemsolarzellen und moderne Charakterisierungsmethoden kennengelernt. Nach Abschluss des Moduls besitzen die Studierenden vertiefte Kenntnisse, um sich mit der photovoltaischen Energieerzeugung in Forschung und Praxis zu beschäftigen.\nDas Ziel des Moduls ist es, das physikalische Verständnis von Solarzellen bzw. Solarmodulen zu vertiefen. Hierfür werden in der Vorlesung verschiedene Typen von Dünnschichtsolarzellen diskutiert. Hierbei werden die Grundlagen der Photovoltaik wiederholt und im Anschluss werden die Eigenschaften verschiedener Absorbermaterialien, Depositionsverfahren und komplexere Solarzellkonzepte wie Tandemsolarzellen vorgestellt. Die Wahlpflichtveranstaltungen bieten die Möglichkeit zur Vertiefung der Kenntnisse, z.B. der grundlegenden physikalischen Prozesse, der Analyse photovoltaischer Materialien und Systeme oder der Herstellung von Solarzellen in Laborpraktika.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Vertiefung Photovoltaik', 'group': '34321800 FG Perowskit-Solarzellen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien'}, {'id': 41172, 'name': 'Vertiefung Photovoltaik intensiv', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Photovoltaik - Dünnschichtsolarzellen und neue Konzepte (PV2)', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien', 'group_str': '34321800 FG Perowskit-Solarzellen', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden besitzen vertiefte Kenntnisse auf dem Gebiet der Erzeugung erneuerbarer Energie mit Hilfe photovoltaischer Systeme. Sie haben ein Verständnis für die grundlegende, physikalische Wirkungsweise von Solarzellen und sind in der Lage die Performance zu analysieren und Strategien zur Optimierung von Solarzellen zu entwickeln. Sie kennen die grundlegenden Verfahren zur Herstellung von Solarzellen und können verschiedene Aufbauten beschreiben sowie deren Wirkungsweise beurteilen. Die Studierenden kennen verschiedene Typen von Dünnschichtsolarzellen, welche auf verschiedenen Absorbermaterialien basieren. Darüber hinaus haben sie komplexere Solarzellkonzepte wie Tandemsolarzellen und moderne Charakterisierungsmethoden kennengelernt. Nach Abschluss des Moduls besitzen die Studierenden vertiefte Kenntnisse, um sich mit der photovoltaischen Energieerzeugung in Forschung und Praxis zu beschäftigen.\nDas Ziel des Moduls ist es, das physikalische Verständnis von Solarzellen bzw. Solarmodulen zu vertiefen. Hierfür werden in der Vorlesung verschiedene Typen von Dünnschichtsolarzellen diskutiert. Hierbei werden die Grundlagen der Photovoltaik wiederholt und im Anschluss werden die Eigenschaften verschiedener Absorbermaterialien, Depositionsverfahren und komplexere Solarzellkonzepte wie Tandemsolarzellen vorgestellt. Die Wahlpflichtveranstaltungen bieten die Möglichkeit zur Vertiefung der Kenntnisse, z.B. der grundlegenden physikalischen Prozesse, der Analyse photovoltaischer Materialien und Systeme oder der Herstellung von Solarzellen in Laborpraktika.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Vertiefung Photovoltaik intensiv', 'group': '34321800 FG Perowskit-Solarzellen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Hochfrequenz und Halbleiter-Systemtechnologien'}, {'id': 41173, 'name': 'Machine Learning 2-X', 'version': 6, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Classical Topics in ML', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}, {'name_part': 'Explainable Machine Learning', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Generative Models', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Hot Topics In ML', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Machine Learning in Neuroscience', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Machine Learning in Science and Industry, Lectures', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Mathematische Grundlagen für Maschinelles Lernen', 'type': 'KU', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Probabilistic Modeling and Inference', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Representations in Machine Learning', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Scientific applications in Machine Learning', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2020', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24795}, {'name_degree': 'Biomedizinische Technik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24814}, {'name_degree': 'Computational Engineering Science (Informationstechnik im Maschinenwesen) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018 (17.01.2018)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24859}], 'exam_type_str': 'written', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Students have in-depth knowledge of the application of specific machine learning methods (classification, regression, dimension reduction, clustering) in selected application areas (bioinformatics, computer security, etc.) and can apply and further develop these methods independently. In particular, students are familiar with the aspects of machine learning that are crucial for practical success.\n\nDepending on the elective course, students can also deepen either their mathematical knowledge, their Python experience or an individually selected application area from machine learning.\nThis lecture deals with advanced topics of machine learning. Special emphasis is placed on the application. Several successful applications of machine learning will be discussed and the specifics of each will be addressed. Topics covered include: semi-supervised learning, boosting methods, optimization theory, kernel methods for structured data, graphical models.\n\nExamples of successful applications include bioinformatics, computer security and text mining.\n\nIn addition, students can choose the following specializations in the compulsory elective course, depending on their previous knowledge and interests:\n\n* Mathematical foundations for machine learning: this course repeats, deepens and specializes the mathematical knowledge from the basic modules of the computer science degree.\n* Seminars: in the respective seminars, students practise the independent incorporation and presentation of scientific results.\n* Machine Learning in the Sciences: in the respective additional lectures, the corresponding topic is further deepened theoretically', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Machine Learning 2-X', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41174, 'name': 'Medizinische Signalverarbeitung', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Medizinische Signalverarbeitung', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Medizinische Signalverarbeitung', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (Lehramt) (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24406}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (Lehramt) (M. Ed.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'L', 'stupo': 24463}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Biomedizinische Technik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24814}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik', 'group_str': '34311900 FG Elektronische Systeme der Medizintechnik', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden haben ein elementares Verständnis der Entstehung, Erfassung und Verarbeitung biologischer Signale sowie der Beeinflussung biologischer Organismen durch Signale. Sie sind befähigt, Systeme zur Erfassung und Verarbeitung elektrophysiologischer und hörakustischer Signale zu verstehen, zu entwickeln, zu verbessern oder auch zu modifizieren.\nIn der Integrierten Veranstaltung wechseln sich Vorlesungen zu physiologischen Grundlagen mit Vorlesungen und Programmierübungen zu signaltheoretischen und algorithmischen Inhalten ab. So werden z.B. die Funktionen des Nervensystems, des Herz-Kreislaufsystems sowie des Gehörs aus elektrotechnischer Sicht betrachtet. Im technischen Teil werden u.a. Möglichkeiten zur Signalerfassung, Filterung, Quellentrennung und zum maschinellen Lernen auf der Basis elektrophysiologischer und akustischer Daten besprochen. Die Programmierübungen in Python zeigen Verfahren zur medizinischen Signalverarbeitung und zum maschinellen Lernen aus elektrophysiologischen und elektroakustischen Signalen. Weiterhin werden medizintechnische Firmen oder Forschungseinrichtungen besucht.\n\nIm Projekt Biosignalverarbeitung definieren sich Gruppen von nicht mehr als zwölf Studierenden ein eigenes Projekt zur Entwicklung einer systemelektronischen Baugruppe oder eines Echtzeitalgorithmus im Bereich der Elektrophysiologie oder der medizinischen Akustik. Das Projekt wird in Arbeitspakete unterteilt, wobei auf Schnittstellenfestlegungen besonders zu achten ist. In Teamarbeit findet die Schaltungsentwicklung, die Programmierung, der Aufbau und Test statt. Die Ergebnisse werden in einem Bericht dokumentiert und am Semesterende gemeinsam demonstriert. Beispiele: EKG-Verstärker mit Auswertung, digitaler Audioverstärker mit Quellentrennung für Hearables, etc. Das Modul enthält auch Inhalte zur gesellschaftlichen Verantwortung und Nachhaltigkeit bzw. zur Technikfolgenabschätzung, insbesondere: - Problem- und Praxisbezug - Zukunftsbezug und Reflexivität - Normativität und Nachhaltigkeit - Inter- und Transdisziplinarität.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Medizinische Signalverarbeitung', 'group': '34311900 FG Elektronische Systeme der Medizintechnik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Energie und Automatisierungstechnik'}, {'id': 41175, 'name': 'Current Topics in Intelligence Research', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Current Topics in Intelligence Research', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352100 FG Modellierung kognitiver Prozesse', 'module_description': 'Acquisition of deeper knowledge in selected current topics of intelligence research. Different topics will be covered in each semester, ranging from algorithms for artificial intelligence (e.g., machine learning, control, optimisation, robotics) to the application of methods from computer science to study biological intelligence (e.g, computer vision for behavioural tracking, computational models of behaviour, machine learning or statistical tools for behavioural data analysis). Students will be able to present and discuss current scientific results and perspectives both orally and in a written report.\nCourse with changing content in the areas of intelligence research. Interdisciplinary focus, combining different perspectives on intelligence from computer science (robotics, control theory, machine learning), natural sciences (ethology, neuroscience) and social sciences (psychology, educational science).', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Current Topics in Intelligence Research', 'group': '34352100 FG Modellierung kognitiver Prozesse', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41176, 'name': 'The AMOS Project - Product Owner Role', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'AMOS - Product Owner Role', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34332300 FG Open Distributed Systems', 'module_description': '- Students learn about agile methods, in particular Scrum and eXtreme Programming (XP)\n- Students gain practical hands-on Scrum experience as a product owner in a team project\nThis course teaches agile methods (Scrum and XP) and open source tools using a single semester-long project. It takes place online and across multiple universities. Topics covered are:\n- Agile methods and related software development processes\n- Scrum roles, process practices, including product and engineering management\n- Technical practices like refactoring, continuous integration, and test-driven development\n- Principles and best practices of open source software development\nThe project is a software development project in which each student team works with an industry partner who provides the idea for the project. This is a practical hands-on experience.\nThis module is for the product owner role.\nSign-up and further course information are available through a Google spreadsheet at https://amos.uni1.de -', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'The AMOS Project - Product Owner Role', 'group': '34332300 FG Open Distributed Systems', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41177, 'name': 'Project Advanced Research Data Infrastructures', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Research Data Infrastructures', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme', 'group_str': '34332310 FG Forschungsdateninfrastruktur', 'module_description': 'The students can explore new and emerging technologies in the area of Advanced Research Data Infrastructures. They can plan and implement a given, practical project of limited size based on some of these technologies. They are be able to decide whether the technologies they explore are useful for a given project. They can also present their progress within the project and create a documentaiton of their project. They are further able to reflect on the outcomes of the project using these technologies.\nIn this module, students will work on a practical project of limited size. For this purpose, a software component related to a given topic is specified, implemented, tested and documented. The topics provided vary from semester to semester, and allow exploring new and emerging technologies of one or more of the following fields:\n\n • Semantic Web, Linked Data and Knowledge Graphs\n • Data Management and Data Infrastructures\n • Quality of Data and FAIRness of Data\n • Language Models, Natural Language Processing\n • Information Extraction, Text Summarization, Question Answering, Recommendation', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Project Advanced Research Data Infrastructures', 'group': '34332310 FG Forschungsdateninfrastruktur', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Telekommunikationssysteme'}, {'id': 41178, 'name': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuits and Systems (AAIC) (12 LP)', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '12', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuit', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuit', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24537}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341200 FG Mixed Signal Circuit Design', 'module_description': 'Der kontinuierliche Fortschritt im Bereich der integrierten nanoelektronischen Schaltungen und Systemen erlaubt es, immer komplexere Funktionalität mit stetig steigenden Arbeitsgeschwindigkeiten in einem Systems-on-Chip Ansatz zu integrieren. Das Modul „Advanced Analog Integrated Circuits and Systems“ greift diese technologische Entwicklung auf und befasst sich mit den analogen Grundschaltungen und Konzepten die für Anwendungsfelder wie Wireless-Infrastruktur Anwendungen (z.B. LTE), Transceiver Systeme für elektro-optische Anwendungen (z.B. Silicon Photonics), verlustleistungsarme Sensorsysteme für biomedizinische Anwendungen (z.B. Nervenstimulation) oder Themen aus der Automobilelektronik oder Internet-of-Things (IoT) grundlegend sind.\nIn diesem Kurs werden die folgenden Themen vermittelt:\n1. High-Speed Transceiver-Architekturen, Betriebsarten und Bausteine\n2. Switched Capacitor-Schaltungen, SC-Integratoren, SC-Verstärker, SC-Filter, Abtastglieder, diskrete Signalverarbeitung\n3. Differentielle OTAs und Opamps, Komparatoren, Übertragungsfunktionen, Versorgungsspannung und Gleichtaktunterdrückung, Metastabilität\n4. Rückgekoppelte Systeme, Nichtlinearitäten, Closed-Loop-Architekturen, Gleichtaktrückführung und deren Architekturen', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 12, 'ects_str': '12', 'name_str': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuits and Systems (AAIC) (12 LP)', 'group': '34341200 FG Mixed Signal Circuit Design', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41179, 'name': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuits and Systems (AAIC) (9 LP)', 'version': 3, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuit', 'type': 'PR', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}, {'name_part': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuit', 'type': 'VL', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341200 FG Mixed Signal Circuit Design', 'module_description': 'Der kontinuierliche Fortschritt im Bereich der integrierten nanoelektronischen Schaltungen und Systemen erlaubt es, immer komplexere Funktionalität mit stetig steigenden Arbeitsgeschwindigkeiten in einem Systems-on-Chip Ansatz zu integrieren. Das Modul „Advanced Analog Integrated Circuits and Systems“ greift diese technologische Entwicklung auf und befasst sich mit den analogen Grundschaltungen und Konzepten die für Anwendungsfelder wie Wireless-Infrastruktur Anwendungen (z.B. LTE), Transceiver Systeme für elektro-optische Anwendungen (z.B. Silicon Photonics), verlustleistungsarme Sensorsysteme für biomedizinische Anwendungen (z.B. Nervenstimulation) oder Themen aus der Automobilelektronik oder Internet-of-Things (IoT) grundlegend sind.\nIn diesem Kurs werden die folgenden Themen vermittelt:\r\n1. High-Speed Transceiver-Architekturen, Betriebsarten und Bausteine\r\n2. Switched Capacitor-Schaltungen, SC-Integratoren, SC-Verstärker, SC-Filter, Abtastglieder, diskrete Signalverarbeitung\r\n3. Differentielle OTAs und Opamps, Komparatoren, Übertragungsfunktionen, Versorgungsspannung und Gleichtaktunterdrückung, Metastabilität\r\n4. Rückgekoppelte Systeme, Nichtlinearitäten, Closed-Loop-Architekturen, Gleichtaktrückführung und deren Architekturen', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Advanced Analog Integrated Circuits and Systems (AAIC) (9 LP)', 'group': '34341200 FG Mixed Signal Circuit Design', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41180, 'name': 'DBPRO - Datenbankprojekt (unbenotet)', 'version': 3, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'DBPRO - Databases Project', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'WS2023', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24544}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'module_description': 'Die Studierenden erlernen die arbeitsteilige Entwicklung eines Informationssystems entlang der klassischen Vorgehensweise von Gesamtsystemspezifikation über die Modellierung, Feinentwurf, Implementierung, Systemintegration sowie Demonstration eines Prototyps des Systems. Weiterhin verfügen sie über ein solides Grundverständnis für Datenmanagementsysteme, das sie befähigt die Lösbarkeit solcher Aufgaben mit den erlernten Techniken zu bewerten. Sie sind darüber hinaus in der Lage, die entsprechenden Kenntnisse und Techniken zielführend anzuwenden\nZu Projektbeginn erhalten Sie eine schriftliche Projekt-Aufgabenbeschreibung, aus der Sie zunächst eine Gesamtsystemspezifikation erstellen. Anschließend erstellen Sie einen Entwurf, die Detail-Spezifikation und schließlich implementieren Sie Komponenten des Systems. Abschließend integrieren und testen Sie das System und stellen Ihre Arbeit im Rahmen einer Systemdemonstration vor. Die verwendeten Technologien sind vom jeweiligen Projekt abhängig. Üblicherweise werden C/C++, relationale und NoSQL-Datenbanksysteme, Indizierungssysteme und Visualisierungssoftware zum Einsatz kommen. Zur Projektdurchführung sollen Sie selbstverantwortlich computergestützte Werkzeuge zur effektiven Umsetzung und Management des Projekts einsetzen, insbesondere zur effizienten Kooperation, zur Source-Code-Verwaltung, zum automatisierten Testen und zur automatisierten Dokumentationserstellung. Der Projektfortschritt wird fortlaufend anhand von Meilensteinpräsentationen überprüft. Am Ende des Projektes sind die Herangehensweise, Ergebnisse und Tests in Form eines Projektberichts zu dokumentieren. Das Projekt wird durch die Systemdemonstration und eine mündliche Rücksprache abgeschlossen.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'DBPRO - Datenbankprojekt (unbenotet)', 'group': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41181, 'name': 'Graduate Research Project DM I', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Graduate Research Project DM I', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'module_description': 'Data management (DM), together with machine learning (ML) is one key driver underlying the current wave of innovation in artificial intelligence and data science. This course is research-oriented and specifically designed for students who wish to get involved in scientific projects within the field of DM from early on in their degree course. Each participating student will work on an individual research-oriented topic in one of the areas of expertise of their advisor in continued discourse with the latter. After successful completion of the course students will have learned how to properly approach and survey a scientific problem in the existing literature, acquired comprehensive knowledge across the relevant field, obtained experience in the quality assessment of research results with respect to precision and reliability, as well as in survey and report writing, and oral presentation of the same. In addition, the early focus on an independent research project promotes critical thinking, organisational, and time management skills.\nResearch problems will be drawn from the current research undertaken by BIFOLD investigators. In order to obtain a general idea of research underway, students should visit the BIFOLD website (https://bifold.berlin/) for the latest information. For more concrete details, students should contact the individual investigator directly.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Graduate Research Project DM I', 'group': '34351500 FG Datenbanksysteme und Informationsmanagement (DIMA)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41182, 'name': 'Graduate Research Project ML I (6 LP)', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Graduate Research Project ML I', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'module_description': 'Machine Learning (ML), together with Data management (DM) is one key driver underlying the current wave of innovation in artificial intelligence and data science. This course is research-oriented and specifically designed for students who wish to get involved in scientific projects within the field of DM from early on in their degree course. Each participating student will work on an individual research-oriented topic in one of the areas of expertise of their advisor in continued discourse with the latter. After successful completion of the course students will have learned how to properly approach and survey a scientific problem in the existing literature, acquired comprehensive knowledge across the relevant field, obtained experience in the quality assessment of research results with respect to precision and reliability, as well as in survey and report writing, and oral presentation of the same. In addition, the early focus on an independent research project promotes critical thinking, organisational, and time management skills.\nResearch problems will be drawn from the current research undertaken by BIFOLD investigators. In order to obtain a general idea of research underway, students should visit the BIFOLD website (https://bifold.berlin/) for the latest information. For more concrete details, students should contact the individual investigator directly.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Graduate Research Project ML I (6 LP)', 'group': '34352000 FG Maschinelles Lernen', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41183, 'name': 'Project Large-scale Data Engineering (benotet)', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '9', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Large-scale Data Engineering', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'module_description': 'In this project module, students will learn how to create prototypes for specific projects, and give high-quality presentations on these prototypes. These aspects are covered with a special focus on the areas data engineering, data management, and machine learning systems.\nThis module is comprised of a project in the large context of big data engineering, i.e., topics related to scalable data and ML systems. In detail, the module is structured as follows:\n\n* Selection of a project\n* Discussion rounds on design, implementation, tests, and experiments\n* Prototype implementation, tests, and experiments\n* 15min oral presentation of the created prototype', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 9, 'ects_str': '9', 'name_str': 'Project Large-scale Data Engineering (benotet)', 'group': '34352900 FG Big Data Engineering', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41184, 'name': 'Machine and Behavior', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Machine and Behavior', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Information Systems Management (Wirtschaftsinformatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'W', 'stupo': 24781}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik', 'group_str': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'module_description': '1. Build and demonstrate an understanding of cutting-edge research at the intersection of Artificial Intelligence and Behavioral Science.\n2. Develop a critical ability to discuss and critique research articles, and to conceptualize new research projects in the field.\n3. Identify appropriate experimental and computational methods and tools for understanding human and machine behavior.\nIn this course, students will be exposed to cutting-edge research in the field of Machine Behavior, which is a field at the intersection of Artificial Intelligence and Behavioral Science. \n\nThe course will involve both a hands-on learning segment on computational social science methods and behavioral science theories and experiments. Students will lead presentations and discussions on a selection of significant papers in the field. Students will also prepare a brief research proposal for a new idea that they present at the end of the semester.\n\nStudents will explore key research in the interdisciplinary field of Machine Behaviour, covering topics such as the impact of AI on cultural evolution, the behavior and reasoning of Large Language Models (LLMs), and how we can build AI to promote cooperation and creativity.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Machine and Behavior', 'group': '34341700 FG Robotik und Bioinformatik', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Technische Informatik und Mikroelektronik'}, {'id': 41185, 'name': 'Communicating Hot Topics in Intelligence Research', 'version': 1, 'language': 'EN', 'ects': '3', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Science of Intelligence: Distilling Discourse into Outreach', 'type': 'SEM', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34351300 FG Neuronale Informationsverarbeitung', 'module_description': 'Acquisition of science communication skills and deeper knowledge in selected current topics of intelligence research. After successful completion, the participants will have 1) gained insight into a selection of ‘hot topics’ from current intelligence research, as presented by international experts, and 2) acquired the fundamental skills for communicating science to lay audiences, exemplary by 3) producing a short podcast episode intended for public release.\nThe module comprises a distinguished speaker series, with six international experts coming to Berlin to give a lecture each. The experts are recruited from the fields of neuroscience, machine learning, robotics, behavioral biology, psychology, and philosophy. Prefacing the distinguished speaker series, the participants will be introduced to the fundamentals of science communication and scientific storytelling. They will then apply the learned knowledge by conducting short interviews in groups with one of the invited experts. Those interviews will be complemented by further interviewing one SCIoI-internal expert with a similar field of expertise. The participants will then, under guidance, write a podcasting script, process the interviews, record their own material, and then finally produce a short science podcast series, with each group contributing one episode. The podcast will be released on common podcasting platforms.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 3, 'ects_str': '3', 'name_str': 'Communicating Hot Topics in Intelligence Research', 'group': '34351300 FG Neuronale Informationsverarbeitung', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 41186, 'name': 'Vertiefende Themen in HCI', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Vertiefende Themen in HCI', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24514}, {'name_degree': 'Elektrotechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24536}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Engineering (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24540}, {'name_degree': 'Computer Science (Informatik) (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'I', 'stupo': 24541}, {'name_degree': 'Technische Informatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2015', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24546}, {'name_degree': 'Medieninformatik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24752}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24836}, {'name_degree': 'Wirtschaftsinformatik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2021', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24921}, {'name_degree': 'Medientechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2022', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24924}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät IV', 'institute': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik', 'group_str': '34353300 FG Mensch-Computer-Interaktion (HCI)', 'module_description': 'Wissen: Die Studierenden haben einen umfassenden Überblick über gutes bzw. schlechtes User Experience Design in der Praxis und dessen Anpassung für XR erhalten, mit individuellen tiefen Einblicken in ein Thema ihrer Wahl.\n\nSkills: Die Studierenden haben die Fähigkeit erworben oder verfeinert, wissenschaftliche Literatur selbstständig zu sichten und systematisch zu strukturieren, und haben Erfahrung darin gesammelt, ihre Literaturrecherche einem kritischen Publikum zu präsentieren sowie an wissenschaftlichen Diskussionen teilzunehmen.\n\nKompetenzen: Die Studierenden sind in der Lage, neue wissenschaftliche Ergebnisse im Bereich der HCI in Praxis und Theorie kritisch zu reflektieren. Sie sind in der Lage, diese Ergebnisse mit der Literatur in Beziehung zu setzen und ihre Qualität und Wirkung anhand geeigneter Maßstäbe zu beurteilen. Sie sind auch in der Lage, bestehende Forschungsergebnisse in eine neue XR-Umgebung zu übertragen. Schließlich sind sie in der Lage, ihre Prototypen mit ersten nutzerzentrierten Untersuchungen zu testen, z. B. mit heuristics.\nEinführung:\n- Grundlagen der HCI (Vorkenntnisse erwünscht)\n- Überblick über die Interaktion in XR\n- Literaturüberprüfung von guten und schlechten Beispielen in Theorie und Praxis (z.B. infinite scrolling)\n- Identifizierung von Metriken aus einer HCI-Perspektive, um Design-Innovationen von der Vergangenheit bis heute kritisch zu diskutieren\n\nGruppenprojekte:\n- Identifizieren Sie in der Gruppe ein Beispiel aus der obigen Einführungssitzung (gute vs. schlechte Designinnovationen) \n- Erstellen Sie drei Low-Fi-Prototypen, wie diese Beispiele auf XR übertragen werden könnten.\n- Diskutieren Sie in der Gruppe, welchen Sie auf der Grundlage der Metriken aus der Literaturübersicht (aus der Einführungssitzung) auswählen sollten.\n- Erstellen eines testbaren XR-Prototyps mittlerer Größe \n- Heuristic Test (oder ein anderer nutzerzentrierter Test) mit den zuvor definierten Metriken \n- Präsentation des Gruppenprojekts und des Prototyps\n- Gruppenportfolio einreichen', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Vertiefende Themen in HCI', 'group': '34353300 FG Mensch-Computer-Interaktion (HCI)', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Softwaretechnik und Theoretische Informatik'}, {'id': 50000, 'name': 'Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung', 'version': 3, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung', 'type': 'IV', 'cycle': 'WiSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Human Factors (MSc) - StuPO 2011', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 21561}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24412}, {'name_degree': 'Automotive Systems (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24775}, {'name_degree': 'Fahrzeugtechnik (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2017', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24812}, {'name_degree': 'Human Factors (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 24815}, {'name_degree': 'Verkehrswesen (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2018', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24819}], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät V', 'institute': 'Institut für Land- und Seeverkehr', 'group_str': '35334100 FG Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung für energetische Optimierung und Unfallvermeidung', 'module_description': 'Umfassender Überblick über aktuelle Methoden der Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung und deren Anwendungsgebiete mit Verknüpfung zu fahrerunterstützenden Systemen. Die Studierenden lernen Prozesse und Randbedingungen zur Entwicklung von Methoden der Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung kennen und werden qualifiziert, selbstständig Systemzusammenhänge zu analysieren, Auswertemethoden zu entwickeln und anzuwenden sowie diese in den Kontext der statistischen Relevanz einzuordnen. Sie entwickeln ein inhaltliches Verständnis für Funktionsweise und Ableitungen aus Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung und können dieses auf zukünftige Entwicklungen im Automobilbau, insbesondere Car2X-Kommunikation applizieren.\nDie Lehrveranstaltung stellt mit engem Bezug zu aktuellen Beispielen und Forschungsvorhaben die Vielfalt der existierenden und in der Entwicklung befindlichen Methoden und Techniken der Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung, deren Komponenten (Messtechnik, Datenbanken, Simulationsmodelle, Protokolle) vor und geht auf die aktuellen Fragestellungen hinsichtlich Anwendungsgebiet (Car2X-Kommunikation, Verbrauchsoptimierung, Unfallvermeidung), Möglichkeiten (Technische Umsetzung, Anwendungsgebiete abseits der Fahrzeugtechnik) und Grenzen (Datenbearbeitung, Datenschutz, Einflüsse der Umgebung) ein. Die Methodik wird zum Teil praktisch erprobt.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung', 'group': '35334100 FG Fahrerverhaltensbeobachtung für energetische Optimierung und Unfallvermeidung', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Land- und Seeverkehr'}, {'id': 50001, 'name': 'Projektwerkstatt Reise- und Sporttretboot', 'version': 1, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Tretboot PW', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [], 'exam_type_str': 'continuous', 'faculty': 'Fakultät V', 'institute': 'Institut für Land- und Seeverkehr', 'group_str': '35331200 FG Entwurf und Betrieb maritimer Systeme', 'module_description': 'Ziel des Projekts  ist die Entwicklung eines neuen Freizeit-/ Sportgeräts.  Es soll ein Boot entstehen, welches leicht zu bedienen und handhaben ist. Ähnlich wie Kanus unterliegt ein Tretboot als muskelbetriebenes Fahrzeug keiner Führerscheinpflicht.\r\nAus Umweltschutzgründen ist das Befahren von vielen europäischen Gewässern mit verbrennungsmotorbetriebenen Fahrzeugen verboten. Dies steigert den Erholungswert. Muskebetriebene Fahrzeuge unterliegen diesen Restriktionen nicht.\r\n\r\nEs ist ein interdisziplinäres Projekt mit Fragenstellungen aus den Bereichen Technisches Design, Konstruktion, Fertigung, Versuchstechnik, Marketing und weiteren Punkten.\r\n\r\nErlangung folgender Kompetenzen:\r\n- Erwerb der Fähigkeit, komplexe Problemstellungen zu erkennen und auszuwerten\r\n- Organisation und Durchführung eines Entwurfs, Konstruktions- und Fertigungsablaufs\r\n- Erwerb der Fähigkeit, Problemstellungen in der Gruppe zu lösen\r\n- Teambildung und Teammanagment\r\n- termingerechte und zielführende Planung von Abläufen\r\n- persönliches Engagement und Eigenverantwortung als Grundlage des Gruppenerfolges\r\n\r\nFachkompetenz: 20%\r\nMethodenkompetenz: 20%\r\nSystemkompetenz: 30%\r\nSozialkompetenz: 30%\nDie Projektwerkstatt ist eine von Studierenden, unter Leitung der Tutoren, weitestgehend selbstständig organisierte Lehr-, Forschungs- und Entwicklungsveranstaltung. Innerhalb des Projektes werden die folgenden Themen behandelt:\r\n\r\n- Festlegung der Hauptabmessungen\r\n- Human Factors Engineering\r\n- Erarbeitung des Marketings für das Produkt\r\n- Erstellung eines Vorentwurfes\r\n- Schiffstheoretische Auslegung eines Rumpfes\r\n- Konzeption und Umsetzung von Ausrüstungskomponenten (Sitze, Tretbock, etc.)\r\n- Konzeption und Umsetzung eines elektrischen Hilfsantriebs\r\n- Erarbeitung eines Sponsoringkonzepts und Öffentlichkeitsarbeit\r\n\r\nDie Studierenden arbeiten sich in Kleingruppen mit Unterstützung durch die Tutoren in grundlegende Themen ein und präsentieren diese in Form von internen und externen Referaten.', 'test_description': '', 'ects_i': 6, 'ects_str': '6', 'name_str': 'Projektwerkstatt Reise- und Sporttretboot', 'group': '35331200 FG Entwurf und Betrieb maritimer Systeme', 'institute_str': 'Institut für Land- und Seeverkehr'}, {'id': 50002, 'name': 'Projekt Modellieren im konstruktiven Leichtbau', 'version': 4, 'language': 'DE', 'ects': '6', 'parts': [{'name_part': 'Modellieren im konstruktiven Leichtbau', 'type': 'PJ', 'cycle': 'WiSe/SoSe'}], 'degrees': [{'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (M. Sc.) - StuPO 2007 (19.12.2007)', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'M', 'stupo': 5721}, {'name_degree': 'Physikalische Ingenieurwissenschaft (B. Sc.) - StuPO 09.01.2012', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 9241}, {'name_degree': 'Technomathematik (B. Sc.) - StuPO 2014', 'semester_degree': 'SS2024', 'bama': 'B', 'stupo': 24379}, {'name_degree': 'Technoma